| ARM-PACKROOT-COMPARISON-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Extend the D-154 R-1/R-2 truthfulness cure to the arm side so the arm-side pack comparisons stop reporting a content difference when only the recorded pack location differs | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Merged via #208 (squash SHA to be recorded at merge): the R-1 freeze-replay comparator was generalised into one shared helper, `_pack_mapping_mismatch_kind`, and both arm-side whole-dict equalities now route through it — the dry-run staleness limb and the consumed-arm authentication in the launch-lineage check — with `pack_root` compared under the same successor-scoped rule (generations ≥ `family_publication_first_generation` repository-relative and still COMPARED, `_v3` and earlier absolute per the 2026-08-20 ruling, lexical validation only, no normcase, non-repo paths still refusing). Details are true per branch; no new reason codes. All four acceptance items met, with mutation kills recorded at both named sites. The independent audit REFUTED the first round on a finding the row's own registration missed: a THIRD whole-record `_pack_record` comparison in `_derive_arm_semantics_for_verification` is production-active via `scripts/launch_window.py` → `_verify_arm_receipt` and DOMINATED both cured sites, so the cure was unobservable through the real launcher. Confirmed at the bench, cured in the last code commit of the series, and ADOPTED by the magistrate: a whole-dict site that DOMINATES both cured sites must be cured or the cure is unreachable through the launcher. The fence's "only the two arm-side comparisons" was the registering sweep's CENSUS, not a limit — the PR #192 refuter found two consumers of the recorded absolute pack_root and this row's audit corrected that census to FOUR (freeze identity, dry-run staleness, arm verification, consumed-arm authentication), all now routed through the single shared helper. The delta re-audit's independent census confirms the comparison-site set is n