   114	| PLANTEST-RGLOB-RACE-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Cure the `checkout_inventory` rglob/scandir race in `tests/test_d117_decode_contrast_plan.py` (run 32745254371: `os.scandir` died mid-walk when a directory vanished during the recursive inventory) | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Closed on verification via PR #203; the CURE had already landed at `a28b55bf` on 2026-08-24, after this row's text was authored. `checkout_inventory` no longer uses `Path.rglob`: it walks with `os.walk(topdown=True, onerror=<re-raise>)` and prunes `.git` and `__pycache__` from `dirnames` before descending, so the git loose-object fan-out directory that vanished under a background repack is never scandir-ed at all. Exactness is deliberately preserved rather than traded for tolerance — a real, non-excluded directory vanishing mid-walk still raises, and the regression says so in as many words. Three deterministic regressions ship with it, driven by `_VanishingDirectoryHarness`, which patches `os.scandir` to pause the walking thread at a chosen directory while a worker thread `rmtree`s it: `test_git_object_store_is_never_walked_and_cannot_toll_the_inventory` (cites the hosted provenance verbatim and asserts the hook never even fires — not firing IS the green result), `test_inventory_raises_when_a_real_directory_vanishes_mid_walk`, and `test_inventory_matches_the_rglob_semantics_it_replaces` (symlinks, dangling links, empty directories). Acceptance evidence: bench, `tests/test_d117_decode_contrast_plan.py` three consecutive runs at `24 passed, 1 skipped, 24 subtests passed` each; hosted, the same 36-run/31-green census recorded on CALEXITS-FOURTH-SHAPE-01 above, in which this race did not recur. Same failure family as the identity-pins teardown race cured on PR #203 and as `EVIDENCE-AUTHOR-GIT-TEARDOWN-01`: a background git process mutating a fixture tree another thread is walking or removing. |
