     1	# The Orchestration Process
     2	
     3	How this project is actually built: a human researcher directing a
     4	multi-model AI system whose workflow is itself a deliberate, versioned,
     5	self-instrumenting piece of engineering. This document is the single
     6	in-repo description of that process. (The executable playbooks live
     7	outside the repository as reusable "skills" so they transfer to future
     8	projects; this page describes what they do and where their evidence
     9	lands in this repo.) Binding role and process changes live in
    10	`docs/decision_log.md`; this page avoids copying volatile model versions.
    11	
    12	## Roles: a lead, independent implementers/reviewers, and a human at the top
    13	
    14	- **Ed (researcher)** sets research direction, methodology
    15	  non-negotiables (raw-evidence bundles, dual-basis capture with gross-energy
    16	  headlines, named
    17	  measurement boundaries, no unauditable claims), hardware/access
    18	  decisions, and — critically — *process policy*: every rule below
    19	  traces to a standing instruction issued after an observed failure or
    20	  opportunity. External-facing claims and merge authority derive from
    21	  him (he granted the lead conditional self-merge authority on
    22	  2026-07-08 once the review gate had proven itself).
    23	- **The designated lead** owns
    24	  decomposition, triage, design adjudication, every final diff gate,
    25	  all live/hardware verification, merge decisions, bookkeeping, and
    26	  process evolution. Other agents save lead capacity without inheriting
    27	  final authority; all escalation paths terminate at the lead.
    28	- **Independent implementation and review agents** do the heavy reading and
    29	  writing: implementation against pinned specs, adversarial review
    30	  lenses, test writing, test *auditing* (never of its own tests — a
    31	  fresh instance audits), docs drafting, and review of the lead's own
    32	  consequential decisions. Cross-model review is load-bearing by
    33	  design: the attributed per-layer catch record (below) shows the two
    34	  roles consistently catching different classes of defect.
    35	- **Specialist agents** handle bounded sweeps (for example, docs
    36	  consistency) and, when a stream genuinely needs
    37	  mid-stream judgment, as a stream director. AMENDED by D-129
    38	  (Ed, 2026-08-09): lieutenant-directed executor lanes are the standing
    39	  default shape under the lead-token economy (current model assignments
    40	  live in D-129 and the memory index, not here) — the "exception rather
    41	  than the default" framing below reflects the C-009/C-010 record of
    42	  its day and is superseded for current operation (see the decision log).
    43	- **Image-heavy analysis uses the designated image-capable review route** per
    44	  C-012, after the site-observatory stream's image-critique rounds.
    45	- **Invited-peer validation is allowed to overturn lead designs**; C-014
    46	  recorded two lead designs overturned by an invited peer before
    47	  implementation.
    48	
    49	## The loop, end to end
    50	
    51	Every substantial session runs one conductor procedure:
    52	
    53	1. **Intake** — read `RUN_STATE.md` (the intake pointer), the task
    54	   queue, the latest run report; never re-decide anything the decision
    55	   log settled.
    56	2. **Decompose** — split work into genuinely independent streams
    57	   (disjoint expected diff footprints), one git worktree + branch each;
    58	   assign each stream a review tier by *cost of being wrong*
    59	   (measurement-semantics and contract-bearing work gets the full
    60	   pipeline; docs get a light tier). Preflight gates: hardware-shaped
    61	   streams require a confirmed device inventory; anything pinned
    62	   without live validation carries a PROVISIONAL label; measurement
    63	   sessions require a no-agent "quiet machine" lock.
    64	3. **Per-stream pipeline** — for each reviewable unit: an invited
    65	   design-argument round (the implementer must argue trade-offs before
    66	   coding), implementation, then a layered review stack:
    67	   2–3 fresh-instance counterreview lenses over the diff → lead triage
    68	   with recorded dispositions → fixes → a dedicated test-amplification
    69	   round (an independent writer adds edge-case tests) → a
    70	   writer≠reviewer test audit (a fresh instance hunts tautological,
    71	   vacuous, or wrong-expectation tests) → the lead's diff gate.
    72	4. **Lead live gates** — never delegated: the lead runs the real flow
    73	   (real corpus, real CLI, real hardware where present). This layer has
    74	   repeatedly caught blockers no other layer saw, including defects
    75	   whose own tests were green because the tests encoded the same wrong
    76	   assumption as the code.
    77	5. **Merge gate** — multi-commit series land as branch + PR. Before any
    78	   merge: a pre-merge oversight pass by 2–3 fresh reviewers with
    79	   distinct angles (deep regression hunt; claim-to-evidence trace;
    80	   merge-order simulation across sibling PRs), lead triage, fixes, CI
    81	   green. **Final-head rule:** any commit that lands after the last
    82	   review round gets one more fresh review before merge — no commit
    83	   merges unreviewed, however small (its first application caught a
    84	   crash path in a "trivial" post-review fix).
    85	6. **Integration review** — after parallel streams merge, one dedicated
    86	   review hunts *interaction* defects no single-stream review can see.
    87	   Its catches are definitionally unique (first outing: two).
    88	7. **Bookkeeping** — a single session record (run report) with a
    89	   verbatim process-trace appendix; the intake pointer and queue
    90	   refreshed; a delegated docs-consistency sweep before the final
    91	   commit (its latest pass found 15 real drift items; earlier passes
    92	   found 5–6). Large documentation batches add the pre-commit
    93	   docs-verify mode; the `consistency-sweep` skill owns that shape,
    94	   including the D-043 supersession check.
    95	8. **Same-session distillation** — lessons fold into the process
    96	   playbooks the same session they are learned. Measured effect: one
    97	   failure mode recurred five times before its fix was distilled, zero
    98	   times after. The current operation-loop also runs its §0
    99	   primary-deliverable check and §8 shipped-check before the session is
   100	   considered done.
   101	9. **Post-landing verification and close-out** — landed work gets the
   102	   matching verification workflow with severity-tiered refuters. Sessions
   103	   that change front-facing state refresh `docs/site/DRIFT.md`; no agent
   104	   regenerates or deploys the site. Automation informs and Ed deploys
   105	   manually, per D-068 and `RUN_STATE.md` end-of-work step 8.
   106	10. **Meta-review (the final step)** — event-driven, not calendar-driven:
   107	    when a review layer stops earning its keep, when an intervention
   108	    repeats despite a folded fix, or when the user asks, the loop is
   109	    reviewed with its own evidence discipline (see Topology for the
   110	    consensus one such review produced). After large workloads the
   111	    post-large-workload meta-reassessment (owned by operation-loop §10)
   112	    always fires, and it runs LAST.
