   114	### Stop cards and paused work
   115	
   116	When a session stops with live work in progress, the lead creates or
   117	updates an `ACTIVE_STOP_CARD` at the top of `RUN_STATE.md`. While active,
   118	that card is the single restart authority and overrides every lower
   119	"what next" list, queue rank, mission guide, and run-report default.
   120	
   121	A stop card must name:
   122	
   123	- the resume authority and exact artifact pointer,
   124	- the reason for stopping,
   125	- worktrees, branches, PRs, and off-repo artifacts that must not be
   126	  cleaned accidentally,
   127	- status terms for each paused item,
   128	- the first resume action, and
   129	- the clearance criteria.
   130	
   131	Use these status terms for paused work:
   132	
   133	| Term | Meaning |
   134	|---|---|
   135	| `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED` | A worker reports code or docs are applied, but the lead has not gated the diff. Not merge-safe. |
   136	| `LEAD_GATED` | The lead has reviewed and run the required local/live checks for the item. |
   137	| `PR_OPEN_CI_GREEN` | A PR exists and CI is green, but merge authority has not yet fired. |
   138	| `MERGED` | The accepted work has landed on main. |
   139	| `UNREAD_UNADJUDICATED` | A report/synthesis exists but has not been consumed into decisions, queue rows, or rejected findings. |
   140	| `ADJUDICATED` | Findings have explicit accept/reject/defer disposition and downstream artifacts are updated. |
   141	
   142	Before an intentional pause, do the minimal stop sync even if full
   143	bookkeeping cannot fit: update only `RUN_STATE.md`'s stop card and the
   144	rank-0 queue row. That is enough to prevent accidental bypass.
