   193	## Council discipline
   194	
   195	Councils are expensive instruments. Use a full council for methodology,
   196	measurement validity, schema/contract changes, claim boundaries, hardware
   197	protocols, or explicit user requests. For ordinary implementation, use a
   198	small number of targeted lenses plus lead adjudication.
   199	
   200	Every high-impact council must leave a durable scorecard:
   201	
   202	- unique catches by severity,
   203	- accepted/rejected/deferred/false-positive counts,
   204	- lead triage and rework time when practical,
   205	- shipped artifacts,
   206	- queue rows created or re-ranked,
   207	- decision-log IDs promoted, and
   208	- a disposition table: finding → ruling → owner → artifact/queue/decision
   209	  target → closure check.
   210	
   211	Deferred decision-log promotion is itself a tracked obligation, not
   212	ambient prose in a report.
