   265	## Topology: how it evolved (an example of the loop improving itself)
   266	
   267	- **v1 (2026-07-07 AM):** per-stream Fable orchestrator subagents, each
   268	  driving its own Codex thread. Worked, but expensive at the apex tier.
   269	- **v2 (2026-07-07 PM):** Opus orchestrators directing Codex, Fable
   270	  apex-only. Ran four streams — and surfaced a structural flaw: subagent
   271	  orchestrators are not woken by their childrens' completion (the "wake
   272	  gap"), forcing the lead to babysit with heartbeats. The session's own
   273	  trace captured two fleet-wide stalls.
   274	- **Meta-review (C-009):** a signed cross-model consensus — two blind
   275	  Codex analyses vs. the lead's blind position, one conferral round —
   276	  produced a hybrid: the lead drives pipeline-shaped streams directly
   277	  (inheriting the harness's only reliable wake guarantee); subagent
   278	  directors are reserved for judgment-heavy streams.
   279	- **Validation (C-010, 2026-07-08):** the first full session under the
   280	  new topology ran ~26 Codex sessions across four streams — resume
   281	  through merge — with zero coordination stalls, zero manual wake
   282	  interventions, and no subagent stream directors at all.
   283	  The consensus is now the stamped default.
   284	
   285	The same mechanism has overturned the lead's own designs: a Codex
   286	review of the lead's process schemas rejected two of them and supplied
   287	better ones (now the v2 ledger and calibration formats), and review
   288	lenses have refuted two of the lead's sanctioned wire-protocol pins
   289	before they could reach hardware. Seniority is not infallibility; the
   290	adjudication of every such challenge remains the lead's.
   291	
   292	## What one session looks like (2026-07-07/08, the merge session)
   293	
   294	Four checkpointed streams resumed, completed, and landed as four PRs:
   295	the integrity/provenance overhaul (all 31 audit-pinned defects fixed;
   296	strict validation now re-derives the power trace from raw evidence),
   297	the docs package, the KV-cache replay feasibility verdict, and the
   298	complete fixture-first NVIDIA stack. The layered review recorded, among
   299	~30 attributed catches: two blockers found only by fresh-instance
   300	lenses (a provenance hash that did not prove the actual generation
