TASK_QUEUE.md:102:| HISTPACK-PROMISOR-NOFETCH-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-28 | Make `_historical_pack_tree` (`joulewise/arm_readiness.py`) fail closed on a blobless or promisor clone: S3 delta re-audit 2 finding D4 found the derivation lazily fetching the four missing historical blobs it needed through the promisor remote and PASSING with 219 still missing | RETIRED UNBUILT by the threat-model prune ruling R-2 (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/threat-model-prune/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md`, the D-161 addendum): all three blind seats classed it as pure clone policing whose only actor is the trusted operator, the guard is already porous, and the saving is the largest of the prune because the cost is unspent; the measurement checkout is a full clone. Sol's implemented diff is custodied unmerged at `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/threat-model-prune/discarded-HISTPACK-PROMISOR-NOFETCH-01.diff` should appetite change. No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Kernel row (A107) removed 2026-08-28 in the T27 second kernel wave. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:104:| HISTPACK-TEMP-CLEANUP-01 | P3 Hardening Candidates | 2026-08-27 | Close the temp-checkout leak in the historical-semantics verifier: a cleanup error raised BEFORE removal left both populated `joulewise-histsem-` scratch checkouts on disk while arm and freeze both refused with `histsem_history_unavailable`, and the committed regression called the real cleanup before raising so it could not see the leak | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #222 (branch `fix/histpack-temp-cleanup-01`; gauntlet: Sol xhigh implement → independent Sol audit (cleanup items 1-3 all MET, `git diff -G 'flagless|allowlist|preserve'` empty) → magistrate ruling R-2 (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/threat-model-prune/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md`) narrowed the branch to this row alone → re-audit + one execution refuter on the reduced diff). CURE (production diff ≈ 10 lines in `_histsem_temporary_workspace`): the yielded scratch path is remembered, and when the `TemporaryDirectory` context raises `OSError` a bounded, subprocess-free `shutil.rmtree(..., ignore_errors=True)` unwinds it BEFORE the existing `histsem_history_unavailable` refusal is raised; no admission or refusal semantics changed, no timeout added, no allowlist widened. REGRESSION (`tests/test_receipt_histsem.py::test_temporary_workspace_cleanup_failure_is_governed_at_arm_and_freeze_boundaries`, corrected to the D3 probe shape): the fake `__exit__` now records that each scratch tree is NON-EMPTY and raises WITHOUT calling the real cleanup, then asserts both trees absent, the parent empty, and both boundaries still refusing with `histsem_history_unavailable`; red against the pre-fix code (`AssertionError: False is not true` — both trees present), green after. Sibling row HISTPACK-PROMISOR-NOFETCH-01 was RETIRED unbuilt by the same ruling; its implemented-but-discarded diff is preserved off-repo by the S13 director only. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:106:| PACKAUTH-PRESERVE-TAUTOLOGY-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Stop preserve mode from making ordinal-1 PACK_AUTHENTICATION a tautology — the echo path re-emits the committed frozen bytes instead of re-deriving them, so `--check` compares those bytes with themselves | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #214 (branch `fix/packauth-soundness-rows`; gauntlet: design consult → implement → independent audit → fix round → delta re-audit → magistrate-authorized fix round 2 → second fresh delta re-audit). WHAT WAS WRONG, executed: with `PRESERVE_CURRENT_FROZEN_BYTES` true the generator's `_generate` writes every output straight from `REPO_ROOT` and RETURNS EARLY — even the pinned external-input drift checks are never reached — so a committed science-row tamper AND an acceptance-JSON drift each pass a preserve-mode `--check` with rc=0 (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/what-check-proves.md`, replayable via `replay-mutations.sh`). CURE, at two boundaries, with no frozen byte and no schema touched. (1) At the evidence author: every generator invocation is classified `regenerated` or `echo`, the preserve selection is EXPLICIT rather than inherited from the generator's compiled-in default, and an `echo` result can no longer produce `pack_generator_check_status: PASS`. (2) At the histsem verifier: an authenticated PACK_AUTHENTICATION item is re-derived at the coordinate its OWN source and receipt already record — source/receipt `head_commit` and `pack_sha256` must agree, that exact local-Git coordinate is materialized in a temporary checkout, and the plan-pinned generator runs there under explicit no-preserve, composed with the existing K5/K12/binding/closed-delta checks. A U11-PROJECTED coordinate uses the composed anchor+replay derivation instead of a bare check: a bare check at a projected coordinate refuses, because the projection rewrites `plan_tree.json`, `plan_tree.sha256` and `producer_contract.json` through a different serializer, and treating those receipts by bare check would have failed the pre-arm gate for the entire `_v4` family. THE HARD PART took two rounds: admitting a flagless generator on an AST NAME SCAN (absence of the identifier `preserve_current_frozen_bytes`) proves nothing, because an echo can be written under any other name — the first delta re-audit executed exactly that attack and watched the classifier label a tamper `regenerated`. Fix round 2 made flagless generators DEFAULT-DENIED, admitted only by exact SHA-256 membership in a closed, minimal allowlist of reviewed historical generators whose digests are derived from local Git at the coordinates the ordinal-1 sources name; the name scan may now only REFUSE, never admit. Regression-pinned at both boundaries: the foreign-identifier echo attack is refused, an allowlisted historical generator still authenticates. Acceptance evidence (a) is `what-check-proves.md`; (b) is the non-tautological derivation plus its regressions, verdict A94 MET by the second delta re-audit (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/delta2/report.md`, no blocker findings). `_v4` re-verified from post-cure code — default-deny is exactly the shape that could have broken it: all three emitting `_v3` generators classify explicit-flag, projected authoring and anchor+replay pass, custody scripts unchanged, 99/99 committed receipts still validate, +2.310 s median per pack. NOT done here, recorded for the magistrate as follow-ups from the second delta re-audit: D2 (the contract narrates echo-vs-regeneration but shows no literal before/after bytes, and `PACK_DIGEST_DOMAIN` and the pre-authoring invariant are used as criteria before they are taught), D3 (a cleanup error raised BEFORE removal leaves the temporary checkout on disk; both boundaries still govern-refuse, and the committed regression cleans up before raising so it cannot see the leak), D4 (a blobless partial/promisor clone lazy-fetched four missing blobs and returned PASS instead of failing closed — a PRE-EXISTING property of `_historical_pack_tree`, newly discovered rather than newly introduced, and the most consequential of the four), and D6 (the reviewed S-1 manifest pins builder digest `29335e6f…` while the current builder and its sidecar agree on `d72c1560…` — the r4 runsheet generates a current BASE manifest so operation is unaffected, but the cited review record is false, which matters for the imminent mint). Custody: `docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/`. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:107:| SUPERSESSION-DUP-REFUSAL-01 | P1 Phase Gate | 2026-08-27 | Rule on and then implement write-time refusal in the supersession recorder, which appended silent duplicate records when run more than once for a member and voided campaign membership downstream | Landed as PR #206 (`36dcdd76`). Ruling-first, as the row required. **D-156** was authored and landed by the magistrate BEFORE any implementation, on a ruling packet (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/supersession-dup-ruling-packet.md`) built from a Sol xhigh read-only design seat plus lieutenant re-verification of every file:line; a blind Fable refuter then returned SOUND on both lenses over D-156's five premises (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/supersession-dup-refuter-fable.md`). Ruled semantics, implemented verbatim: any *recognizable* row (exact `record_type` OR exact `schema_version`) already carrying this `bundle_id` in the **target log** refuses, keyed on `bundle_id` within one log, checked inside the held `campaign.lock` BEFORE the candidate row is constructed and before quarantine bytes are read — and **presence, not validity, occupies the slot**: a recognizable-but-invalid row refuses just as hard, because an invalid competing disposition must never license a second one. Refusal surface follows the `LaunchLineageError` precedent: `SupersessionRecorderError(ValueError)` carrying `.reason_code`, validated against a **sibling** registry `SUPERSESSION_RECORDER_REASON_CODES` (deliberately NOT a widening of `LAUNCH_LINEAGE_REASON_CODES`, so the paper's disjoint-vocabulary claim at `docs/paper/draft-v1.md:742` stays true), wire values `campaign_occurrence_supersession_already_recorded` and `campaign_occurrence_supersession_log_unreadable`, printed through the one existing `error: {reason_code}: {msg}` path at exit 2. The refuter's R-1 residual was real and material: the guard's first draft read `load_campaign_log_rows`, which *tolerates one recognized final tear*, while the consumers re