TASK_QUEUE.md:108:| FROZEN-RECEIPT-CONSTANT-STALE-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Stop successor-family PACK_AUTHENTICATION from resting on `CURRENT_FROZEN_RECEIPT_SHA256`, the generator constant that names the PREDECESSOR's freeze receipt | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #214 (branch `fix/packauth-soundness-rows`; gauntlet: design consult → implementation → independent audit → fix round → delta re-audit). The staleness is structural, not an accident: `embedded_generator_bytes()` emits a successor generator by substituting only `CURRENT_FAMILY_SUFFIX`, so every successor family is born one generation behind and `_v4` — emitted from the `_v3` generators — will name the `_v2` freeze-0002 digest too. Executed across all nine packs (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/characterization.md`, replayable via `replay-characterization.sh`): the three ordinal-1 packs match their own receipt and pass a bare `--check`; all six successors exit 1 with `generation failed: the current frozen identity requires preserve mode`. ADOPTED RULING: the constant is NOT refreshed per generation and the authentication path stops depending on it. Refreshing is impossible rather than merely undesirable — a successor generator is emitted before its own freeze receipt exists, so the digest it would need does not yet exist, and editing the generator after the mint would change already-frozen pack bytes (D-153 would then force a new family generation). The ruling is recorded normatively in `docs/contracts/receipt_histsem_verifier.md` §'Adopted A93 ruling' (dated 2026-08-26) and pinned by `test_frozen_receipt_constant_variants_do_not_change_the_authentication_verdict`, which holds one derivation fixed, varies the constant through absent / matches-current / names-predecessor / unrelated / computed / duplicated / malformed forms and requires an IDENTICAL authentication verdict with only diagnostic differences. The constant is now read by a TOTAL `ast.parse`/`ast.literal_ev