3623:### The baseline pin, the fleet, and the drift question
3639:### The fleet outcome: 11/11 returned, and the single READY did not survive
3643:The blockers concentrate where the charter's new seats were pointed. **L8 (operator/recovery) returned seven** — the largest single-seat yield in the T-series — led by B1: the T-0 evidence author "consumes nine byte-canonical JSON inputs that no tool, no runbook step, and no packet step produces; the only 2am path forward is hand-fabricating canonical JSON with invented monotonic_ns values, which the receipts cannot distinguish from honest capture." **L6 (seam reader A) independently found the same gap** from the producer-consumer side, and added B2: every one of the frozen packs' generic evidence receipts is already past its 24h monotonic horizon, so "any arm receipt issued now is expired at birth." **L1 (authority plane)** confirmed the expiry against all 33 receipts and added B2, the kernel fail-open: `active_global_gates: []` while `RUN_STATE` renders "READY — Q2 P2-006" for a campaign D-117 superseded — "a quiet night gets spent on a campaign whose outputs do not trace to the current claim path, bypassing the council gate entirely." **L10 (the sacrificial lifecycle seat the consult's F5 bought)** executed the after-window path and found it unbuilt: `analyze-claims` refuses the packs' own `v3.prospective` manifests, the designed prospective builder/validator do not exist, "the window is spent and its REQUIRED OUTPUT cannot trace through a claim consumer without landing new code post-hoc." **L4** produced the charter's named type specimen: the margin recorder REFUSEs the re-specced frozen spec with `authoritative_input_invalid`, while "the committed census tests model 'real floor pack cell shapes' WITHOUT the estimator vocabulary, so the suite is green while the real seam is broken." **L9** found both arm-time census probes unpassable on the real machine — permanently resident Apple daemons match the maintenance census, and the browser/monitor regexes match nine always-resident Safari LaunchAgents and `watchdogd` — with the diagnosis of why CI never saw it: "tests fake the probe executor with exit_code=1."
3647:### The refuter round: nine xhigh lenses, three kills, two new defects, and seven hours lost to relays that never launched
3651:**The relay wedge is the process finding.** The first wave launched four runs at 2026-08-14 23:25 PT; the other **five refuter relay agents wedged for roughly seven hours reading bridge-contract documentation without ever launching their Sol runs**, and were killed at 07:15 PT the following morning and relaunched from the lead shell per the T5 lesson. The relaunched five — `A-execution`, `B-contract`, `B-execution`, `ECF-contract`, `ECF-execution` — started within 37 seconds of each other at 14:15Z and **all five finished inside 13 minutes** (423 s to 760 s each, manifest-verified). Seven hours of wall clock bought thirteen minutes of work that a lead-shell launch delivered immediately. The standing rule is now third-time-confirmed: runs that matter launch from the lead shell, and `.status` is not liveness.
3661:Everything else was **CONFIRMED, several with executed refusals**: the 33/33 expiry refusals reproduced at live monotonic; `load_manifest` refusing `v3.prospective` verbatim; the margin recorder's `authoritative_input_invalid` on the forbidden `estimator_registration` key at the pack-pinned spec cell; the prewindow dwell measured at **60.09 s against the author's required 600 s**; all four env/chain mismatches. Several remedies were corrected rather than accepted — in-place re-author is **not** contract-valid under D-131 (a successor pack + custody root is required), the 24h horizon is implementation policy rather than contract text, F1+F2 merge into a single shipped T-0 acquisition tool, and F3's remedy is a minimum dwell in `--wait`, **not** a lowered author threshold. Refuters earned their spend on both edges: they killed three claims that would have generated work orders against nothing, and they found two defects that would have reached the night.
3663:### The cold pairing: four blockers against the sitting itself, all cured before recording
3670:- **B2 — mandatory packet contents were incomplete.** A 23-finding consistency sweep (7 blockers / 10 should-fix / 6 nits) was compressed into one line plus a sha16 of an uncustodied file, and "the only one shown is the one the reviewed party killed." Three omissions bore directly on the sitting: sweep-B1 (a doc anchored at T4-late asserting NO-GO for closed gates — a **false-dirty** generator inside the pinned baseline, the exact mirror of the false-clean risk the sitting was ordered to adjudicate), sweep-S3 (the M-2 remedy "describes a regeneration that deliberately did not happen" — withheld from the pairing asked to rule on M-2), and sweep-B5 (stale kernel — independent corroboration of L1-B2 that the packet did not record as corroborated). "A packet whose visible triage of an input consists of the single finding the reviewed party refuted is not 'mechanically assembled' in the rule-11 sense." Cured: the full sweep is custodied with per-finding triage state.
3680:### The verdict: NOT-READY, 0/11, and a program that is not certified complete
3688:The ratified program runs in four phases. **Phase 0 (rulings and consults before code):** R1 freeze-evidence lifecycle — durable-freeze-evidence vs successor-pack tool, rule-2 design consult mandatory, and its own cold gate if it amends contract text; R2 `FROZEN_PLAN` identity; R3 P2-006 retirement; R4 the M-2 execution-note amendment plus the remanded M-2 cold gate; design consults for the prospective-manifest validator/finalizer and the margin-recorder authorization; L8-B7's launcher binding recorded as contract-bearing. **Phase 1 (parallel code):** WO-KERNEL-RECONCILE first and magistrate-supervised (it edits the declared sole work-selection authority — lieutenant-forbidden alone); the integrated WO-T0-PRODUCER (nine-input capture tool, ≥10-min dwell, the D-127 privileged clock route landed at last, env/chain/manifest plus the doubled-plan-path fix with a real-pack regression, and the terminal-review-trailer producer with its second lens first); WO-LAUNCH-BINDING; WO-CONSUMPTION-EDGE; WO-MARGIN-RECORDER-AUTHZ; WO-CENSUS-SEMANTICS (hard-gated on ED-Q-L9-3's quiet-state fixture); WO-DETECT-PULSES-BUDGET; WO-L2-REAUDIT; and a should-fix batch carrying the sweep's verify-and-fix items including B7, the paper's 8.611855 J vs 1.869502 J floor-regime contradiction, registered as a **live P1 claim-bearing queue row**. **Ed-required, one batched session:** D-127 sudoers install with explicit ratification (it amends D-004's privilege posture), the **full dress rehearsal E-4→E-9 plus author→arm→verify→consume against scratch custody — "the program's single most valuable Ed hour"** — the sampler checklist, SIGTERM relay and rail probe, the keyboard-backlight rows, ED-Q-L9-3 early because it gates the census work order, production-machine freeze-chain replays, the §5C live verification, the a9/a10 desk replay, and the decisive network replay. **Phase 2 (sequential):** the re-freeze via the R1-ruled route, **once, atomically, LAST among pack-byte changes** — this is Opus W2, "the sharpest omission," because the re-freeze rotates the pack digests and therefore destroys the very baseline manifest that produced the audit; irreversible, so magistrate + Ed — regenerating truthful freeze-aware status text and thereby retiring M-2; then the successor arm packet, only after the T-0 repair passes end-to-end at the exact reviewed head. **Phase 3:** baseline-manifest supersession with the ruled fields, focused re-audit of the pack/custody-bearing seats, adversarial coverage re-enumeration of every universe, delta re-audits per C-028 on every fix round. **Phase 4:** a reconvened READY-CANDIDATE sitting with a fresh cold pairing.
3690:**Four findings are labelled SINGLE-LENS** and may not drive implementation until a second distinct lens reads them: L2-1, L2-COV-1, L2-EDQ-1 (all from the one falsely-clean run, which itself had an environment gap) and the terminal-review-trailer gap (B-execution only). "Lead relay corroboration of counts is not a distinct lens." That second refuter was launched by the magistrate at verdict recording (`run_started` 2026-08-15T14:44:05Z, xhigh, read-only) and **completed eight minutes after the custody commit** — rc 0, `OK`, valid envelope, 472 s, overall `NOT_READY`. It read an independent EXECUTION lens over **exactly the four SINGLE-LENS claims** and returned **three CONFIRMED, one PARTIAL** — which discharges Disposition 5 on all four, pending custody. **L2-COV-1 CONFIRMED** and hardened: the crash matrix is 13 tests not 16, the omitted three-window module holds 23, "the eight-module direct universe is exactly 251 tests." **L2-EDQ-1 CONFIRMED**: three 600-second loaded-host failures are durably recorded, WO-CRASHMATRIX-RELIABILITY is open, live writer/sudo qualification is unexercised. **The terminal-review-trailer gap CONFIRMED**: the author requires three exact trailers, `ac3fe1d` carries none, and repository search finds consumers and tests but no operational producer. **L2-1 PARTIAL** — the `detect_pulses` projection genuinely has no enforced cell, deadline or cancellation budget and genuinely runs synchronously under the writer lease, but the *literal* non-convergence framing is refuted: "the unbudgeted tree is finite but intractably large." Remedy sharpened rather than overturned — a deterministic evaluation budget with registered fail-closed finalization, plus a bypass of full projection when the clock anchor is already unresolved. **CUSTODIED at `15d00d2`** (magistrate, same day): the report landed in `refuter-outputs/sol-refuter-singlelens.md` with a council-verdict addendum discharging Disposition 5 and clearing all four SINGLE-LENS labels — the custody lag was eight minutes, not a recurrence of the B1 defect class.
3692:### Process rulings entered at this sitting
3694:**A charter amendment, adopted at the pairing — the correct venue for a proposed process rule.** Opus S12 found charter:77-78 ("only T0 rows may remain open at the sitting") both violated (23 ED-QUALIFICATION rows open, none performed) and **unsatisfiable as written**: the fleet is what *enumerates* the ED-QUAL universe, so those rows could not have pre-existed it. The rule is impossible on a first sitting — a charter defect, not a compliance failure. Amending it is "any proposed process rule," a rule-11 mandatory item, so the pairing itself was the correct venue. Adopted: sittings divide into **ENUMERATING** sittings (first-pass; output includes the ED-QUALIFICATION universe; charter:77-78 does not bind) and **READY-CANDIDATE** sittings (charter:77-78 binds). This sitting is recorded as an ENUMERATING sitting.
3706:### Unique catches by layer
3710:- **The C-028 refuters (nine xhigh lenses):** they earned their spend on both edges. **Kills:** L8-B4 (both lenses, executed canonical-path counter-probe — a wrong-path artifact, and the refusal it triggered is *correct* fail-closed behaviour), WO-L2-4 (phantom work order that would have made the runbook mislead), and F4's timing premise. **New defects no seat found:** the **doubled plan-path** — production-only and *masked by the test fixture's bare filename*, the second occurrence this span of a suite green over a broken real seam — and the **terminal-review-trailer producer gap**, discovered by noticing that the audit's own baseline commit lacks trailers the T-0 author demands. Plus remedy corrections that would otherwise have shipped wrong: in-place re-author is not D-131-valid, and F3's cure is a minimum dwell rather than a lowered threshold. (Evidence: `refuter-outputs/refuter-verdicts.md`; `sol-refuter-B-contract.md` F6; `sol-refuter-B-execution.md`.)
3711:- **The fleet lenses (eleven seats, 46.7 minutes):** ten of ten gating seats falsified their own readiness. The catches no single-plane review would have produced: **L8** found that the machinery the arm-author gauntlet hardened has **no producer for its own nine inputs** ("the only 2am path forward is hand-fabricating canonical JSON"); **L6 and L7, independent from launch, converged on the same seam from opposite sides**; **L10**, the sacrificial seat, spent a synthetic window and found the claim edge unbuilt before a real window paid for the discovery; **L4** produced the charter's own type specimen — "the suite is green while the real seam is broken"; **L9** found both arm-time census probes unpassable on the real machine and named why CI never saw it (the tests fake the probe executor). The seat-level lesson: **the fleet's yield came from seats that execute against the live machine and the frozen bytes, not from seats that read code.**
3713:- **The consistency-sweep scout — and the scout's own false positive.** The sweep found 23 findings, of which sweep-B1 (a T4-late-anchored doc asserting NO-GO for closed gates, sitting *inside* the pinned audit baseline as a false-dirty generator), sweep-B5 (stale kernel — independent corroboration of L1-B2) and sweep-S3 (the M-2 remedy describing a regeneration that deliberately did not happen) are all material and all fed the sitting. But **its top blocker was itself refuted**: sweep-B4 claimed the baseline manifest's three pack digests "reproduce under no algorithm and match no revision," having recomputed under six candidate algorithms; the digests reproduce **exactly** via `joulewise.arm_readiness.committed_pack_tree_sha256`, verified by the magistrate and re-verified independently by both cold seats. The scout's proposed remedy — overwrite the manifest's digests — would have corrupted the audit's reference artifact. Recorded as the scout layer's cost of doing business: a review layer that reaches for a canonical algorithm and picks the wrong one produces the highest-severity finding shape in the audit, pointed at the audit itself. The cold ruling's counter-catch is the durable part: the false blocker exists **because the manifest names no digest algorithm**, so the fix is a `pack_digest_algorithm` field at supersession, not a scolding. (Evidence: `consistency-sweep-findings.md` B4 + magistrate verification note; cold §G.1; Opus N4.)
3714:- **The drafting mechanic (this entry's own layer):** the two ⚑ OPEN flags. Both became the sitting's two formal dispositions; both were **confirmed by the magistrate rather than argued down**; both were then materially corrected by the pairing (drift survived on a substituted proof, M-2 was remanded rather than closed); and together they are the evidence base for the same-signature structural finding that produced three standing process consequences. A read-only agent verifying a magistrate's dictation against primary evidence found the magistrate's two open process defects. The dictated-fills pattern also produced the span's smaller catch: the T6 merge-count correction from eight to seven (#138 belonged to T5/C-057), landed at `18ef535`. (Evidence: `c058-draft.md` ⚑ items; `magistrate-dispositions-for-sitting.md`; Opus S13.)
3717:- **Lens A (contract):** the acid test that calls the library rather than the mandated CLI (`:707`) — the same defect class as T5's `test_common_mode_full_cli_path_…` stub, a test whose name promises a path it does not take. **The class now has its third and fourth occurrences this span** (L4's green census tests over a broken recorder seam; the doubled-plan-path fixture using a bare filename). It is a class, not a coincidence — see follow-ups. (Evidence: `armauth-lensA-out.md` F1.)
3720:- **The metrology investigation (JW-MET-1):** a paper-side claim overstatement — system-on-chip wording over a CPU+GPU+ANE measurement — found by a question about keyboard LEDs. The sitting produced its sibling: L11's paper-integrity findings and sweep-B7's floor-regime contradiction (8.611855 J vs 1.869502 J), now a live P1 claim-bearing queue row. Claim-bearing prose is audited by no code lens, and it has now yielded a finding in three consecutive spans. (Evidence: `kbd-power-out.md` JW-MET-1; `31ccef5`; cold §F.)
3723:**The pattern worth binding forward:** C-057's lesson was *a second reader of the same bytes*. This span sharpens it — **the highest-yield readers were the ones reading a different plane than the one under construction** — and the sitting supplies the strongest instance yet. The consult read the audit's authority structure while the magistrate designed its component list. The delta read the clock while the fix round read the code. The integration tree read the CI environment while three branches read their own diffs. The metrology run read the paper while everyone read the harness. And **the cold pairing read the sitting's own paperwork — custody, packet assembly, adjudicability, program ordering — while every other layer read the instrument.** Ten gating seats produced sixteen blockers about the machine; two cold seats produced four blockers about whether the verdict about the machine was worth anything. Both were necessary; only one of them was scheduled by anybody's instinct.
3725:### Deliberation resolutions and dissent
3735:### Process findings and follow-ups
3737:**The ~60-minute subagent-shell kill cap did not recur.** C-057's dominant tooling loss — four runs dying at 59.8–60.0 minutes with a `run_started` and no `run_finished` — has **zero occurrences** in this span: all eight manifested implementation runs recorded a `run_finished`, and the longest (`armauth-out`, 54.8 min) sat just under the cap. The mid-session operating rule adopted in T5 (long runs launch from the magistrate's own shell) is consistent with this outcome, but the improvement is **correlational at this sample size** and one run came within five minutes of the old failure mode **[UNVERIFIED-BY-MECHANIC]**.
3754:- **"The test name overstates its proof" is now a confirmed class, not a coincidence** — T5's B1, this span's lens-A F1, L4's green census over a broken recorder seam, and the doubled-plan-path fixture's bare filename. Four occurrences across three spans. It wants a **mechanical check** (real-artifact fixtures for any test whose name asserts a full path), not a reviewer's attention. This is the single highest-leverage process item in the follow-up list.
3756:**Yield/spend:** **Implementation lane:** 8 `codex-run-v3` manifests dated 2026-08-14/15 UTC, recording **8 `run_started` attempts at 2 xhigh / 6 high** and **8 `run_finished` — 5 at rc 0, 3 at rc 65, 0 at rc 79, zero attempts leaving no `run_finished`**; all attempt 1, no retries; aggregate recorded run time **16,804 s** (≈4 h 40 m), longest `armauth-out` 3,288 s. **Six further Sol reports carry no manifest**, so the span's true Sol implementation/review count is **at least 14** and that aggregate is a floor. **Audit lane:** the eleven-seat fleet (`wf_29eee330-1db`) — **2,411,618 subagent tokens, 1,083 tool uses, 46.7 minutes wall, 11/11 returned**; **nine C-028 refuter runs at Sol xhigh, read-only, `write_scope: []`, `head_start 8937dec`**, of which eight are manifested (aggregate recorded refuter run time **4,828 s**, ≈80.5 min; five of those ran concurrently from the lead shell and all finished within 13 minutes) and one (`A-contract`, relay-launched) left no manifest; plus a **tenth xhigh refuter** (the ordered SINGLE-LENS second reader) launched at verdict recording, completed rc 0 in 472 s, custodied at `15d00d2`. **Adjudication lane:** two cold seats (fresh Fable adjudicator + Opus contract refuter) at ~184k tokens, and two Opus drafting mechanics at ~322k **[UNVERIFIED-BY-MECHANIC — magistrate-dictated; the Agent tool leaves no on-disk spend artifact]**. Magistrate context spend likewise leaves no artifact **[UNVERIFIED-BY-MECHANIC]** — the known custody gap, now flagged in four consecutive entries (C-056, C-057, the T6 report's attestation item 4, and here).
