   377	## D-005: One bundle per repetition, grouped by experiment manifest
   378	
   379	- Date: 2026-06-09
   380	- Status: accepted
   381	- Phase: 2+
   382	
   383	Context: `workload_profile.repetitions` exists in the config schema but
   384	nothing defined whether N repetitions produce one bundle or N bundles.
   385	
   386	Options considered:
   387	
   388	1. One bundle containing N sub-runs. Pro: one directory per experiment. Con:
   389	   every artifact (trace, events, summary) needs an internal rep dimension;
   390	   the "bundle = one measured run" invariant breaks; partial failure of rep 3
   391	   of 5 makes bundle status ambiguous; reducers get conditional logic
   392	   everywhere.
   393	2. One bundle per repetition, plus an experiment manifest
   394	   (`runs/experiments/<experiment_id>.json`) listing member bundle IDs, the
   395	   shared config hash, and creation time. Pro: bundle invariant stays "one
   396	   bundle = one measured run = one status"; per-rep failure is naturally
   397	   isolated; Phase 4 aggregation walks manifests. Con: more directories; the
   398	   manifest is one more artifact to maintain.
   399	
   400	Decision: option 2. Bundle IDs of members are `<experiment_id>__r<N>`.
   401	
   402	Considerations: the strongest argument is statistical hygiene in Phase 4 -
   403	each repetition is an independent observation with its own quality fields
   404	(thermal drift, dropped samples), and forcing that independence into the
   405	directory structure prevents accidental cross-rep contamination in reducers.
   406	Partial experiments (3 of 5 reps succeeded) stay representable without a
   407	special bundle state.
   408	
   409	Consequences: controller gains an experiment loop (Slice 2F); cooldown gates
   410	between reps live at the experiment level; `run_bundle_layout.md` documents
   411	the manifest.
   412	
   413	Revisit when: never expected; this is structural.
   414	
   415	---
