   417	## D-006: Dashboard v1 is a static HTML report generator
   418	
   419	- Date: 2026-06-09
   420	- Status: accepted
   421	- Phase: 2 (v1), 4 (figures)
   422	
   423	Context: the original Phase 2 checklist said "dashboard v1 as a read-only run
   424	browser" with no definition. Any web stack is a large dependency and
   425	maintenance surface for a single-user research artifact.
   426	
   427	Options considered:
   428	
   429	1. Flask/FastAPI web app. Pro: interactive. Con: server process, dependency
   430	   tree, session management for zero concurrent users; classic capstone time
   431	   sink; violates "polish after vertical slice" rule in spirit.
   432	2. Jupyter notebooks only. Pro: flexible. Con: not a "run browser"; execution
   433	   state is not reproducible evidence; poor handoff artifact.
   434	3. `python3 -m joulewise report runs/ --output report/` generating static
   435	   HTML: an index table of runs plus a per-run page with metadata, summary
   436	   metrics, and a power-trace chart with phase shading. Charts rendered by
   437	   matplotlib (Agg) to PNG/SVG. No JavaScript build, no server; open the
   438	   files in a browser.
   439	
   440	Decision: option 3. Matplotlib becomes the first real dependency, isolated in
   441	the `[analysis]` extra (D-009), which Phase 4 needs regardless.
   442	
   443	Considerations: the dashboard's actual job in this project is (a) sanity-check
   444	runs during data collection and (b) show the supervisor progress. Static
   445	generation serves both, is testable (assert files exist and contain expected
   446	strings), and produces committable artifacts. Interactivity has no identified
   447	user.
   448	
   449	Consequences: Slice 2J implements it; `report` fails with a helpful message
   450	if matplotlib is missing; notebooks remain available for exploration but are
   451	never the source of report figures (see Phase 4 plan).
   452	
   453	Revisit when: a real interactive need appears (e.g., live monitoring of long
   454	sweeps in Phase 3) - and then prefer extending the generator before adopting
   455	a server.
