   538	## D-009: Dependency policy: stdlib core, optional extras
   539	
   540	- Date: 2026-06-09
   541	- Status: accepted
   542	- Phase: all
   543	
   544	Context: the repo is zero-dependency by design ("Phase 1 can run without
   545	dependency installation"). Phases 2-4 need MLX (Mac runtime), matplotlib
   546	(reports/figures), and likely pandas (aggregation).
   547	
   548	Options considered:
   549	
   550	1. Add dependencies to core as needed. Con: `python3 -m joulewise run` on a
   551	   bare machine stops working; CI and the mock path inherit heavy installs;
   552	   the Phase 5 "new user runs one local benchmark from the README" promise
   553	   gets harder.
   554	2. Keep core stdlib-only forever. Con: re-implementing plotting/dataframes is
   555	   absurd.
   556	3. Stdlib-only core (schemas, controller, mock adapters, bundle writer,
   557	   reducer v1, CLI), with extras: `[mac]` = mlx, mlx-lm; `[analysis]` =
   558	   matplotlib (+ pandas when Phase 4 lands); `[yaml]` = pyyaml (when D-007
   559	   triggers). Adapters import their backend lazily and return structured
   560	   `runtime_unavailable` / `telemetry_unavailable` failures when the extra
   561	   is absent.
