   615	
   616	## D-011: `summary_metrics.json` is the bundle completion marker
   617	
   618	- Date: 2026-06-09
   619	- Status: accepted
   620	- Phase: 2+
   621	
   622	Context: a crashed or killed run must be distinguishable from a completed one
   623	by artifact inspection alone.
   624	
   625	Options considered:
   626	
   627	1. Write into `runs/<id>.partial/` and rename on completion. Pro: atomic.
   628	   Con: a crash leaves `.partial` dirs whose artifacts (events up to the
   629	   crash) are exactly what you want to inspect, but tooling now needs to know
   630	   two names; rename breaks any open file handles on some platforms.
   631	2. A `_COMPLETE` sentinel file. Pro: explicit. Con: one more artifact that
   632	   says nothing else.
   633	3. Define the writing order so `summary_metrics.json` is always written last,
   634	   after all other artifacts are flushed, and define "complete bundle" as
   635	   "directory containing a schema-valid `summary_metrics.json`". The final
   636	   event in `events.jsonl` is `run_finalized`.
   637	
   638	Decision: option 3.
   639	
   640	Considerations: the summary is already mandatory and already last in data-flow
   641	order (it is derived from everything else), so the invariant costs nothing.
   642	`validate-bundle` (Slice 2E) checks it; aggregation (Phase 4) skips
   643	directories without it and logs them as incomplete. Failed runs still get a
   644	summary (status=failed) per D-012, so "incomplete" specifically means
   645	"harness died", which is the signal we want.
   646	
   647	Consequences: bundle writer enforces write order; reducers never run on
   648	incomplete bundles.
   649	
   650	Revisit when: never expected.
   651	
   652	Amendment (2026-07-07, P2-013 group 4, C-007 resolution 2): "schema-valid
   653	`summary_metrics.json`" is now enforced by ONE shared summary validator
   654	used by both `BundleReader.is_complete()` and default validation
   655	(`_check_summary`), with required keys per status: a `succeeded` summary
   656	must carry the headline energy fields present AND finite (audit finding
   657	B1 showed a status-only succeeded summary previously counted as complete
   658	and valid, hiding truncated metrics); token-derived and idle-subtracted
   659	metrics stay nullable; failed/unsupported summaries keep their looser
   660	per-status requirements. "Complete" therefore means "contains a summary
   661	that satisfies the per-status contract", not merely "parseable JSON
   662	object". Historical bundles are unaffected: real corpus summaries
   663	already carry the full field set.
   664	
   665	Superseded in part (2026-07-15, WO-002/R3; D-043): a no-idle-baseline
   666	reduction may remain SUCCEEDED with `energy_request_j` null under the
   667	R3 DISTINCT absent-energy admission state — the succeeded-summary
   668	predicate accepts it while every claim gate requiring request energy
   669	fails closed on that state. The 2026-07-07 shared-validator amendment's
   670	finite-energy requirement no longer binds that one admission state; see
   671	`docs/reviews/2026-07-13-comprehensive-audit/packets/ed-rulings.json`
   672	R3 and the WO-002 canonical predicate.
   673	
