   250	   single process. Con: GIL interaction with an in-process runtime (MLX
   251	   generation) can distort sample timing; threading bugs are the classic
   252	   source of flaky harnesses; the controller would be doing work during the
   253	   measured window (see D-013).
   254	2. `asyncio` event loop. Pro: no threads. Con: forces async contracts onto all
   255	   adapters for one use case; same in-process timing concern.
