  4320	P0). Rulings:
  4321	
  4322	1. **Corner-composed two-edge envelope (P0 repair).** The calibration fits
  4323	   independent start-edge and stop-edge emission lags; a single common trace
  4324	   shift under-covers because independent endpoint errors move energy by up
  4325	   to `2·P·B_fiducial` even when a common shift cancels. The claim envelope
  4326	   is now the extrema over start = `delta_common + eps_on`, stop =
  4327	   `delta_common + eps_off` with `|delta_common| <= B_bundle` and
  4328	   `|eps_on|, |eps_off| <= B_fiducial` independent. For nonnegative power the
  4329	   energy is monotone in each edge separately, so exact extrema are attained
  4330	   at the four edge corners with the common shift scanned continuously — the
  4331	   existing breakpoint-exact scan run per corner. The per-edge corner offset
  4332	   is `±(B_fiducial + wall_minus_monotonic_span)`: the span is a third
  4333	   disjoint per-edge error source, folded into the corners (delta-review
  4334	   amendment) rather than the frozen arms' cruder `2·span·maxP` additive
  4335	   term, and the composed `anchor_bound_s` = `B_bundle + B_fiducial + span`
  4336	   governs the tail-sufficiency gate identically. Idle-subtracted and
  4337	   per-token envelopes additionally widen by `2·(B_fiducial + span)·P_idle`
  4338	   because independent edges vary the subtracted idle duration (delta
  4339	   re-audit catch). New registered method spelling for the 0.5.2/0.6.2
