  4390	### D-078 amendment — 2026-07-21 (third): provenance authentication rulings
  4391	
  4392	Recorded by the lead after confirmation round 2 over `233e9e3` withheld
  4393	sign-off (9 confirmed; the physics verified clean from every lens — all
  4394	findings are provenance/governance). Rulings, implemented in the round-3 fix
  4395	wave (frozen 0.5.1/0.6.1 replay semantics unchanged throughout):
  4396	
  4397	1. **Declared facts are authenticated against primary bytes.** The
  4398	   calibration's declared `capture_wall_time_s` must agree (±1 s) with the
  4399	   capture time independently derived from the hash-verified source events —
  4400	   a stale calibration can no longer be relabeled fresh (the P0).
  4401	2. **Freshness covers the whole measurement.** The 24 h horizon binds both
  4402	   `run_started` and the measured window END: `capture <= run_started` and
  4403	   `window_end <= capture + max_age_s`, inclusive. Pre-run delays cannot
  4404	   carry sampling past the declared validity of its calibration.
  4405	3. **Version identity is validated generically.** Generic bundle validation
  4406	   checks `reducer_version` against the closed known set and the §8.1
  4407	   version/event-semantics pairing rules as a validation-time structured
  4408	   problem (no wire-schema enum — frozen-arm byte replay preserved); an
  4409	   unsupported `--reducer-version` yields the standard structured refusal,
  4410	   never a traceback.
  4411	4. **Stored verdicts are re-derived, never trusted.** The whole-window
  4412	   verifier rejects duplicated NEG-8 core members (occurrence-count
  4413	   semantics) and re-derives the bracket verdict from member evidence;
  4414	   disagreement with the stored row is `whole_window_verdict_conflict`.
  4415	   Delta-review strengthening (lead ruling): the re-derivation tolerances
  4416	   come from the repo-REGISTERED campaign policy whose file hash matches the
  4417	   row's `policy_sha256` — the one trust anchor that does not terminate at
  4418	   bundle custody. Unknown policy hashes, and rows whose self-asserted
  4419	   tolerances disagree with the registered policy, refuse
  4420	   `whole_window_verdict_provenance_invalid` before re-derivation. The
  4421	   custody boundary is otherwise explicit: a forger with bundle write access
  4422	   can rewrite row-internal hashes consistently, but cannot mint a matching
  4423	   tracked policy file.
  4424	5. **Protocol identity is shape-authenticated.** A v2 `protocol_id` requires
  4425	   the v2 estimator identity, capture/horizon fields, and v2 residual shape;
  4426	   v1-shaped bodies relabeled v2 refuse `instrument_calibration_invalid`.
