  7605	## D-115: Quiet-guard Q2 setup authority is a FIXED INSTALLATION CAPABILITY, not general root authority (Commit-1 packet entry; renumbered from the contract's proposed D-114 marker)
  7606	
  7607	**Date:** 2026-08-05 (lead adjudication, Fable magistrate session).
  7608	**Status:** ADJUDICATED under Ed's standing Q2 license (2026-08-05
  7609	ratification batch: Q2 proceeds on lead defaults subject to Ed veto).
  7610	**Numbering note:** the Commit-1 worker proposed this entry as D-114
  7611	inside `docs/contracts/quiet_guard.md` (it does not own the decision
  7612	log, correctly). D-114 was consumed the same day by the T3-CHAIN
  7613	DESCOPE, so this entry is D-115; the contract marker renumbers to
  7614	D-115 in the Commit-1 fix round. **Packet-letter deviation, ruled:**
  7615	the IMPL-PACKET file map places this entry in Commit 1's delta, but
  7616	the branch forked before D-114 landed and an in-branch append would
  7617	manufacture a merge conflict in this file; the entry lands on main and
  7618	is merged back into `impl/quiet-guard`, which satisfies the packet's
  7619	purpose (binding authority exists before the capability merges) with
  7620	cleaner custody.
  7621	
  7622	**Question.** Q2 asked what authority the one-time
  7623	`scripts/setup_quiet_guard.sh` sudo session exercises when it creates
  7624	the root-owned quiet-guard state under
  7625	`/Library/Application Support/JouleWise/quiet-guard/`.
  7626	
  7627	**Ruling.**
  7628	1. **Capability boundary.** The setup script exercises a fixed
  7629	   installation capability: create the root-owned state/install
  7630	   directories, install the fixed-command privileged helper and the
  7631	   narrow `sudoers.d` command aliases, and write `live_promotion=false`.
  7632	   It confers NO general root authority; nothing outside that
  7633	   enumerated set is licensed. Normal guard operation is `sudo -n`
  7634	   against the fixed command aliases only, and the helper drops to the
  7635	   invoking uid/gid before any agent child executes.
  7636	2. **Binding conditions on the capability** (from the 2026-08-05
  7637	   adversarial audits qg-audit-A/B; the capability is not validly
  7638	   exercised without them):
  7639	   a. **Fresh interactive authorization** — the installer must
  7640	      invalidate any cached sudo timestamp (`sudo -k`) before
  7641	      requesting authorization, so a cached ticket can never silently
  7642	      convert repository state into root-executed code.
  7643	   b. **Authenticated content** — what is installed must be
  7644	      authenticated against pinned digests of the reviewed artifacts
  7645	      (or an equivalently strong provenance check), not merely parsed
  7646	      for syntactic validity; root-staging closes copy races but does
  7647	      not authenticate what was staged.
  7648	   c. **Real interpreter isolation** — the installed helper runs with
  7649	      genuine isolation guarantees (no site initialization, no
  7650	      user-site, no environment hooks: `-I`-equivalent), matching the
  7651	      contract's isolation claim.
  7652	3. **Inactive by construction.** Commit 1 installs INACTIVE:
  7653	   `live_promotion=false`, `arm` refuses (`t3_char_pair_verdict_missing`),
  7654	   and no launcher, chain, watcher, or projection code is in scope
  7655	   (D-114 descope). Activation requires a separate, later, Ed-visible
  7656	   step and is not licensed by this entry.
  7657	
  7658	**Consequences.** The Commit-1 fix round renumbers the contract marker
  7659	and implements conditions 2a-2c with discriminating regressions; the
  7660	QUIET-GUARD-01 row cannot land while any condition lacks enforcement.
