  7746	## D-118: NOTHING APPROACHES MERGE WITHOUT THE FULL COUNCIL — the merge gate is enumerated and mechanically checked (Ed directive)
  7747	
  7748	**Date:** 2026-08-07 (Ed, in-thread, verbatim: "make sure they get a
  7749	comprehensive fable pass, and make sure NOTHING gets near merge status
  7750	ever again without the full council..."). **Status:** RATIFIED — apex
  7751	authority; binds every future session and every agent role.
  7752	
  7753	**Trigger (recorded honestly):** three D-117 units (PRs #111/#112/#113)
  7754	merged the same day after a strong but INCOMPLETE gate. They received
  7755	paired audit lenses, lead-written FIX contracts, fix rounds, delta
  7756	re-audits, second fix rounds, second deltas, lead-replayed full suites,
  7757	and green CI. They did NOT receive: (a) the apex Fable diff gate — the
  7758	magistrate substituted test evidence and spot-checks for reading ~9,200
  7759	merged insertions; (b) the mandatory overbuild/merge-ability prune lens
  7760	(Ed's own standing addition); (c) Opus counter-review, which Ed had
  7761	explicitly asked to be in the instrument mix; and (d) for U4, the
  7762	final-head rule — its L5 fix landed after its delta and was merged with
  7763	no fresh pass. Gaps (a)-(d) were self-reported by the magistrate on Ed's
  7764	direct question, then closed retroactively.
  7765	
  7766	**THE GATE (all of it, every time; no item is discretionary):**
  7767	
  7768	1. **Independent audit** of the implementation by a fresh reviewer that
  7769	   did not write it. Never self-graded.
  7770	2. **PAIRED LENSES, distinct angles** — minimum contract + execution.
  7771	   Measurement-adjacent work adds the physics/causality lens.
  7772	3. **Lead-written FIX contract** with dictated closure shapes; findings
  7773	   are triaged and dispositioned, never silently applied.
  7774	4. **DELTA RE-AUDIT of every fix round** — fix rounds introduce defects;
  7775	   this project has proven it repeatedly, including twice on 2026-08-07,
  7776	   where BOTH units' original defect classes survived round one in new
  7777	   forms and only the delta caught them.
  7778	5. **Same-signature statement required** from every delta. A surviving
  7779	   class fires the escalation trigger: the next spend is a consult, not
  7780	   another fix round.
  7781	6. **OPUS COUNTER-REVIEW** on the near-final head — cross-model
  7782	   diversity, not a second Sol pass.
  7783	7. **APEX FABLE DIFF GATE** — a Fable-class judgment pass that READS THE
  7784	   CODE and answers design-level questions (is this the right shape or a
  7785	   workaround frozen into a contract; would a maintainer want to own it).
  7786	   **This MAY be delegated to Fable subagents** (Ed, same exchange:
  7787	   "you can delegate fable missions to other instances of fable") — the
  7788	   magistrate owns the ADJUDICATION of their findings, not the reading.
  7789	   What may never happen is the gate being skipped or downgraded to a
  7790	   cheaper model tier.
  7791	8. **OVERBUILD / MERGE-ABILITY PRUNE** — "would I want to maintain this
  7792	   diff"; surplus abstraction and test bloat are pruned BEFORE merge, as
  7793	   no downstream layer re-asks it.
  7794	9. **Lead full-suite replay, unpiped, on the INTEGRATION tree** (not the
  7795	   stale branch), with the exact tail recorded.
  7796	10. **FINAL-HEAD RULE** — any commit landing after the last review round
  7797	    gets one more fresh-eyes pass before merge, however small. No
  7798	    exceptions; this rule previously caught a live crash path here.
  7799	11. **CI green on the final head**, and for a multi-unit wave, a
  7800	    **post-merge cross-unit integration review** hunting interaction
  7801	    defects no isolated layer can see.
  7802	
  7803	**Mechanical enforcement (so this is not memory-dependent):** every PR
  7804	description must carry a GATE LEDGER listing items 1-11 with the
  7805	evidence path or commit for each, and any item marked NOT-RUN blocks the
  7806	merge. A PR without a complete gate ledger is not merge-eligible
  7807	regardless of CI state. The D-072 self-merge authority is CONDITIONED on
  7808	this ledger being complete — it was never a license to merge on green
  7809	alone.
  7810	
  7811	**Scope note:** a burn/liberal-delegation license (Ed, 2026-08-07)
  7812	increases the volume of work fed INTO this gate. It never reduces the
  7813	gate. If throughput and gate completeness conflict, throughput yields.
