  7815	## D-119: Claim-LANGUAGE rulings delegated to the magistrate, conservative-by-default, until Ed joins the draft loop
  7816	
  7817	**Date:** 2026-08-07 (Ed, in-thread, after the operator-attested
  7818	adjudication: "it's a language issue not a software/hardware issue. yeah
  7819	rule conservative on those, fable i trust you to rule on that for now
  7820	until i start being in the loop on drafts"). **Status:** RATIFIED.
  7821	
  7822	**What is delegated.** How a claim is WORDED — the strength of a
  7823	provenance/custody statement, whether a result is described as
  7824	demonstrated vs designed, how a limitation is framed, which verb a
  7825	guarantee gets. The magistrate rules these directly and records them,
  7826	without waiting on Ed.
  7827	
  7828	**The standing rule for those rulings: CONSERVATIVE BY DEFAULT.** When
  7829	two honest phrasings are available, take the weaker one. An overclaim in
  7830	front of a metrology-expert advisor costs credibility that is expensive
  7831	to rebuy; an underclaim costs a sentence. Where a stronger phrasing is
  7832	actually warranted by evidence, it may be used — but the evidence is
  7833	named in the same breath.
  7834	
  7835	**What is NOT delegated** (unchanged, still Ed's): what to MEASURE, what
  7836	to fund with quiet nights, scope decisions, venue and calendar, anything
  7837	irreversible, and any ruling that changes what the project claims to
  7838	have DONE rather than how it says it.
  7839	
  7840	**Boundary case that prompted this:** the floor artifact's custody
  7841	statement. The finding was that the paper implied third-party
  7842	verifiability where the system provides tamper-evidence within a
  7843	single-operator trust model. No measurement, instrument, calibration, or
  7844	datum was affected — the fix was wording. That class is now magistrate
  7845	territory.
  7846	
  7847	**Termination:** this delegation ends when Ed begins reviewing drafts
  7848	directly. He may reverse any ruling at any time; none of them bind him.
  7849	
