  7851	## D-120: D117-POSTCOLLECTION-TRUST-01 — the postcollection trust closure (adopted consult design, executed)
  7852	
  7853	**Date:** 2026-08-07. **Status:** ADOPTED (design), EXECUTED on
  7854	`impl/d117-postcollection-trust` (merge gated by D-118).
  7855	
  7856	**The defect class (three prior relocations):** the v2 generalized mint
  7857	authenticated postcollection custody pins against
  7858	`component.report["floor_mint_postcollection"]` — a block nothing in
  7859	production emits, so in production both the pins and their "authority"
  7860	would be authored by the same operator hand. Rounds 1-3 each moved the
  7861	trust boundary down a level without terminating it (fabricated-hash
  7862	mint; presence-only check; per-field equality against the same
  7863	operator-authored block).
  7864	
  7865	**The adopted shape (binding design memo: final block of
  7866	`docs/process_traces/2026-08-07-d117-u-units/ESCALATION-CONSULT-RESPONSE.md`):**
  7867	1. `floor_mint_postcollection` is DELETED from production and fixture
  7868	   vocabulary; no producer is assigned; a report containing it (or any
  7869	   unknown key) REFUSES under a closed D-117 mint-consumption profile.
  7870	2. The mint verifies every pin against its DOMAIN OWNER and treats the
  7871	   extraction report as a cache requiring reauthentication, never an
  7872	   oracle. Verifier calculation is mandatory; pin generation is
  7873	   forbidden (missing pins refuse).
  7874	3. The mint derives project commit/tree state by running git itself and
  7875	   refuses a dirty tree; origin/main containment of the mint commit is
  7876	   recorded evidence (unknown tolerated, never a gate).
  7877	4. Every v2 artifact carries the REQUIRED assurance qualifier
  7878	   (`single_authority_hash_bound_replay.v1`, independent_attestation
  7879	   false) stating what the system establishes and does not establish.
  7880	5. The honest trust claim is single-authority, hash-bound, fail-closed
  7881	   consistency — never operator independence (ADJUDICATION-TRUST-MODEL.md
  7882	   controls; the paper's §5/§11 language updated in the same change).
  7883	
  7884	**Consequence:** the v2 mint remains BARRED from issuing until the
  7885	executing branch passes the full D-118 gate and merges; U10 depends on
  7886	this entry.
