  3758	### Source cautions
  3759	
  3760	- **The sealed packet's §2 seat table is STALE against its own §9 and against the verdict.** It still shows L2 READY and the aggregate "1 READY / 10 NOT_READY." The authoritative aggregate is **0 READY / 11 NOT-READY** in `council-verdict.md`; the packet index says so explicitly. A reader quoting the sealed packet's table will get the wrong verdict.
  3761	- **The fleet's aggregate coverage (219/253 across eleven seats) is arithmetic over self-nominated denominators and is NOT an audit-coverage figure.** The one denominator adversarially tested went from a claimed 16 to a real 251. Both cold seats ruled every other denominator suspect for exactly this reason. Do not quote 219/253 as coverage; the honest statement is that coverage is unquantified pending the Phase-3 re-enumeration.
  3762	- **The manifest gap narrowed but did not close, and it moved.** The pre-fleet span has **six** unmanifested Sol reports — `armauth-lensA-out`, `armauth-lensB-out`, `armauth-delta-out`, `armauth-delta2-out`, `charter-consult-out`, `kbd-power-out` — all review/delta/consult runs, effort tier, duration, WRITE_SCOPE and rc unrecoverable **[UNVERIFIED-BY-MECHANIC]**. In the audit lane the ratio inverts: **8 of 9 refuter runs are manifested**, with only relay-launched `A-contract` missing. The class is therefore not "review runs don't manifest" but "**runs launched from inside subagent shells lose their audit trail**" — the same root cause as the rc-74 worktree-vanishing class above.
