   486	### Shape (orchestration decisions)
   487	
   488	- **Decomposition — 5 implementation streams + 1 audit stream, parallel:**
   489	  the queue held independent, file-disjoint tasks; worktree-per-stream
   490	  isolation makes collision structurally impossible (checked against
   491	  expected `git diff --stat` footprints before fan-out). Sequential would
   492	  have serialized ~15-min Codex rounds behind each other for no safety gain.
   493	- **Model assignment:** Fable for stream orchestrators — each stream needs a
   494	  judgment GATE (final-diff review, finding triage, commit decision), not
   495	  volume analysis. Codex 5.5-high for all implementation/review/test volume —
   496	  near-limitless quota makes redundant fresh-eyes passes free, and fresh
   497	  Codex instances carry no thread state, so a fresh instance is a genuinely
   498	  independent reviewer even of Codex's own code. (Gen-1 launch violated
