h and the machine is quiet; scoped by D-162 G2). Fence: No separate live family and no diagnostic generation kind before the campaign: Path A is deferred to PIPELINE-SMOKE-TIER2-01 (R-1); the desk script is the one small code deliverable and changes no production gate (R-3) (D-162 rulings R-1 and R-3). Fence: The G2 block runs on the shakedown's own non-claim runs root (B-3): nothing from it enters any claim or floor, and a custody copy is not relocated (inputs.py:736-784) (D-162, what the seats proved (B-3 shakedown runs root; custody copies are not relocatable)). Fence: The calendar stands (R-4): estate 11 + G1 Fri 08-28; shakedown + G2 Sat 08-29; campaign from Sun 08-30 with G3 nightly (D-162 ruling R-4 (calendar)). Note: Registered 2026-08-27 in the 2026-08-27 T26 end-of-sprint kernel wave (docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/WAVE-ROWS.md) per D-158 R-6 as the ~20-minute quarantined live family generation. RE-SCOPED 2026-08-28 in the T27 second kernel wave per D-162 (docs/process_traces/2026-08-28-live-smoke/proof-consult/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md): two seats proved from code that a partial run on the real _v4 pack can never answer for a DATA reason (insufficient_complete_blocks and fixed_n_plan_incomplete are CONTRACT-classed; the prospective finalizer requires ten blocks / 80 members) and that the diagnostic-family alternative costs 7-10 Sol-days of new admission code on the mint path days before the campaign, so the D-158 R-3 / D-160 R-2 scope is superseded by G1/G2/G3; the D-158 R-3 fences fall with it (magistrate ruling 2026-08-28 on this wave: G2 runs under Ed's T27 live-window authorization as scoped by D-162 G2; the D-158 R-3 diagnostic license is not carried over). D-164 moves the real pack to the _v5 Qwen3 pack, so G2 now starts only after the S15 generator delivers it (event dependency), and the shakedown runsheet is re-cut from PR #225's phases to G2 (R-2). G1 and G3 are desk work; G2 runs on the shakedown night, which keeps the quiet_mac lane and Ed's 