ible half-widths come from the artifact's own admissible_half_widths_j with _validate_estimate_math recomputing the corner from that same array (detection_floor.py:3106), and complete governed campaign membership is not enforced (inputs.py:1522 proves only that artifact-listed members occur in order, never the converse). E3 has no consumption-path regression at all. LEAD-EXECUTED PROOF that the reviewed repository pinset is inert against the artifact: six single-field mutations of mint1.json supplied through the explicit pinset route against the real frozen pack df-ph-decode-floor-mint1.json all returned an empty finding list, including operative_floor_six_decimal 7.377086 -> 9.999999 and extraction_spec_members 30 -> 999; _project_floor_mint_pinset_v2 validates those pins for pinset-internal consistency and then returns only family_identities and evidence_root_ids (detection_floor.py:2059, :2601). The cheap cure (compare the artifact's floor to the pinned six-decimal literal) was proposed by the lead and REFUTED by the design consult with a repro: scaling one component's widths by 0.99999999 moves the exact operative floor 7.377085735735073 -> 7.377085672752914, both rendering as 7.377086, and a non-maximizing width can change with no floor change at all - so floor-literal comparison can never discharge E2's 'any stored width mismatch'. LIVE REMAINDER: strengthened A + B per design-consult D6 - (A) widen the pinset projection to carry the v2 component-artifact digests and exact member dispositions and compare them against the artifact inside validate_floor_artifact; (B) accept per-root governed extraction-spec evidence at claim consumption, authenticate it against the v2 pin, replay floor_extraction, and compare replayed members/widths/corners/floors before populating bound_cell_ids. RESIDUAL (i) for a post-_v4 named decision: E1 is NOT discharged by the pinset route - E1 requires binding to the extraction report and source-member disposition, or rederivation, and 