TASK_QUEUE.md:661:| A96 | EPOCH-LINT-01 | P2 Next Slice | READY [AGENT] | Build the mechanical epoch lint that synthesis R-5 orders: a checker run over a runsheet revision that validates the three dependency kinds the $TRANS producer/consumer sweep cannot see - (i) SYMBOL EXISTENCE at the executing head (every test method, class, constant or function a step greps for or names must exist in the git object at the commit that step runs against, not merely somewhere in the repository), (ii) CONTRACT-REQUIRED CLI INPUTS at every invocation (every consumer call site supplies every argument its authenticator requires - the F3 class, where a digest-conditional path is reachable but no --expected-confirmation-digest or table path is passed), and (iii) FILE LINE COORDINATES (every cited line range still names the whole symbol it claims at the head the citing step reads). Runs at every future runsheet revision. | Runsheet revisions are mechanically checked for non-existent symbols, missing contract-required CLI inputs, and stale line coordinates before they are ratified. Evidence: The lint runs over the S-0 runsheet at a named executing head, reports findings in all three dependency kinds, and exits nonzero on any finding; Replayed against the pre-cure heads it reproduces BOTH motivating cases: the F0-F3 fixation family (kinds i and ii) and the joint-audit B1 join drift (kind iii); The check is wired into the runsheet-revision procedure so no future revision is ratified without a clean run, and its clean run is transcript evidence. Authority: [D-153 sweep magistrate synthesis R-5 (epoch-lint work order, adopted from the Opus seat's generalization)](docs/process_traces/2026-08-24-d153-sweep/03-MAGISTRATE-SYNTHESIS.md). Acceptance: [EPOCH-LINT-01 acceptance](docs/process/state_kernel.json). Fence: Lint only: the checker reports and refuses, it never edits a runsheet - a finding is cured by the ordinary revision path with its own authority (D-153 sweep synthesis R-5). Note: Regis