INE-SMOKE-TIER2-01 registered post-_v4 with the design constraints recorded there)](docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/smoke-corpus-consult/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md#rulings). Acceptance: [PIPELINE-SMOKE-TIER2-01 acceptance](docs/process/state_kernel.json). Fence: Evidence-path rulings are made only after a seat has executed the path or proven from code that it cannot; this row's design claims are executed, not assumed (D-160 ruling R-5). Fence: No synthetic clean leg before the _v4 night and no floor-rule relaxation; the desk smoke before the night is W-11 (#211) plus Unit B, proving contract defects fail loudly, not a clean pass (D-160 ruling R-1). Fence: Path A is NOT built pre-campaign; it lands only here, post-campaign, as the substrate of the permanent desk clean leg (D-162 ruling R-1 (Path A deferred to PIPELINE-SMOKE-TIER2-01)). Fence: The tier-2 replay seam is not CLI-reachable at HEAD and costs two custody surfaces; both are gated on the authenticated smoke generation kind, never on a bundle-level reason (the mock-telemetry lock was withdrawn) (D-158 addendum A-1 / A-2 (the mock-telemetry lock withdrawn; the clean leg's corpus must be produced by the real collector)). Note: Registered 2026-08-27 in the 2026-08-27 T26 end-of-sprint kernel wave (docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/WAVE-ROWS.md) per D-160 R-4 with its constraints carried into the acceptance verbatim in substance. Sequenced post-_v4 by ruling. The desk smoke and its mutation legs (PR #211) are W-11 as landed; PIPELINE-SMOKE-01 proper (the real collector producing the clean leg's corpus on the smoke pack via the fake-collector seam) is the next S10 deliverable per the D-158 addendum A-2 and is not this row. AMENDED 2026-08-28 in the T27 second kernel wave per D-162 R-1: the diagnostic-family path (Path A) that the corrected live-proof gate declined to build pre-campaign moves into this row's acceptance; PIPELINE-SMOKE-LIVE-01 is re-scoped to G1/G2/G3 and carries no family design. |
