  3735	### Process findings and follow-ups
  3736	
  3737	**The ~60-minute subagent-shell kill cap did not recur.** C-057's dominant tooling loss — four runs dying at 59.8–60.0 minutes with a `run_started` and no `run_finished` — has **zero occurrences** in this span: all eight manifested implementation runs recorded a `run_finished`, and the longest (`armauth-out`, 54.8 min) sat just under the cap. The mid-session operating rule adopted in T5 (long runs launch from the magistrate's own shell) is consistent with this outcome, but the improvement is **correlational at this sample size** and one run came within five minutes of the old failure mode **[UNVERIFIED-BY-MECHANIC]**.
  3738	
  3739	**A new envelope class: `SCOPE_CAPTURE_FAILED` (rc 74), caused by the launcher's own worktree vanishing.** Three refuter runs launched from *agent* worktrees (`.claude/worktrees/agent-…`) returned rc 74 with `head_end: null` — the harness deleted the worktree under the running Sol process, so post-run scope capture had nothing to compute against. All three had `scope_action: capture_failed_preserved`, and one (`refuter-L2-out`) additionally returned `report_parse: invalid`, `semantic_status/completion: unknown/unknown`. **All three were harvested from disk anyway, and their content drove the sitting's single most consequential change — the felling of L2's READY.** The five runs relaunched from the lead shell into scratchpad trees returned `OK` uniformly. This is the strongest instance yet of the standing rule that **`run_status` is a statement about the envelope, not about the work**; it is also a concrete argument for launching any run whose output must outlive its launcher from the lead shell.
