  3726	
  3727	The charter consult's rejection was accepted **in full and without negotiation** — thirteen amendments adopted, no partial adoption, no recorded magistrate dissent, and the rejected draft retained on disk rather than deleted. Where the consult and the magistrate's draft disagreed on the verdict form, the consult won outright: READY-WITH-CONDITIONS was deleted rather than tightened, and magistrate-alone READY was replaced by a mandatory cold pairing — the magistrate voluntarily surrendering adjudication authority over its own readiness verdict, months before the verdict existed to be surrendered.
