TASK_QUEUE.md:102:| HISTPACK-PROMISOR-NOFETCH-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-28 | Make `_historical_pack_tree` (`joulewise/arm_readiness.py`) fail closed on a blobless or promisor clone: S3 delta re-audit 2 finding D4 found the derivation lazily fetching the four missing historical blobs it needed through the promisor remote and PASSING with 219 still missing | RETIRED UNBUILT by the threat-model prune ruling R-2 (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/threat-model-prune/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md`, the D-161 addendum): all three blind seats classed it as pure clone policing whose only actor is the trusted operator, the guard is already porous, and the saving is the largest of the prune because the cost is unspent; the measurement checkout is a full clone. Sol's implemented diff is custodied unmerged at `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/threat-model-prune/discarded-HISTPACK-PROMISOR-NOFETCH-01.diff` should appetite change. No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Kernel row (A107) removed 2026-08-28 in the T27 second kernel wave. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:103:| T0-ENV-PARSER-UNIFY-01 | P1 Phase Gate | 2026-08-27 | Unify the exact T-0 `window.env` parser and repair the post-ARM launch-path handoff without widening its 25-key contract | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #221 (branch `fix/t0-env-parser-unify-01`; gauntlet: pinned-spec implementation → defect-shaped regressions → requested CI-equivalent suites; independent review and final gate owned by the director). WHAT WAS WRONG: capture enforced all 25 keys while the evidence author tolerated missing and unknown keys, and the runbook told the operator to add two paths that capture refused. WHAT CHANGED: the one parser and key object now live in `joulewise/arm_readiness_evidence_t0.py`, already inside the T-0 authoring identity; capture and author still translate failures to their unchanged `evidence_author_t0_capture_environment_invalid` and `evidence_author_t0_<kind>_underivable` codes; the runbook derives and exports `ARM_RECEIPT` and `LAUNCH_MANIFEST` after ARM and guards both in the chain; the former skipped regression now passes and every missing/unknown key fails closed at both boundaries. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:105:| BRACKET-BINDING-CLI-01 | P1 Phase Gate | 2026-08-27 | Build the missing fail-closed producer for the finalizer's `--bracket-binding` file and install the producer-before-verdict lifecycle | Producer, evaluator, and finalizer code landed via #217 (`cfffce95`): `scripts/build_bracket_binding.py` builds from the finalized ledger session, frozen plan identity, evidence root and exact runs root without reading a verdict; `scripts/run_campaign.py --whole-window-verdict` consumes the immutable binding and publishes the exact verdict output; the finalizer replays the ledger and requires byte-identical binding/verdict identity, with exact-runs-root and tamper regressions. This PR installs D-160 R-3′'s H5a-before-H5-step-1 order and the campaign/analysis/transaction/claims layout. One placement item is explicitly RULING PENDING: merged code requires the binding and verdict row beneath `$RUNS_ROOT` before the transaction seal, although the addendum described analysis outputs as outside that sealed root; the finalized manifest remains under `$ANALYSIS_ROOT`, and claims go under sibling `$CLAIMS_ROOT`. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:106:| PACKAUTH-PRESERVE-TAUTOLOGY-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Stop preserve mode from making ordinal-1 PACK_AUTHENTICATION a tautology — the echo path re-emits the committed frozen bytes instead of re-deriving them, so `--check` compares those bytes with themselves | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #214 (branch `fix/packauth-soundness-rows`; gauntlet: design consult → implement → independent audit → fix round → delta re-audit → magistrate-authorized fix round 2 → second fresh delta re-audit). WHAT WAS WRONG, executed: with `PRESERVE_CURRENT_FROZEN_BYTES` true the generator's `_generate` writes every output straight from `REPO_ROOT` and RETURNS EARLY — even the pinned external-input drift checks are never reached — so a committed science-row tamper AND an acceptance-JSON drift each pass a preserve-mode `--check` with rc=0 (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/what-check-proves.md`, replayable via `replay-mutations.sh`). CURE, at two boundaries, with no frozen byte and no schema touched. (1) At the evidence author: every generator invocation is classified `regenerated` or `echo`, the preserve selection is EXPLICIT rather than inherited from the generator's compiled-in default, and an `echo` result can no longer produce `pack_generator_check_status: PASS`. (2) At the histsem verifier: an authenticated PACK_AUTHENTICATION item is re-derived at the coordinate its OWN source and receipt already record — source/receipt `head_commit` and `pack_sha256` must agree, that exact local-Git coordinate is materialized in a temporary checkout, and the plan-pinned generator runs there under explicit no-preserve, composed with the existing K5/K12/binding/closed-delta checks. A U11-PROJECTED coordinate uses the composed anchor+replay derivation instead of a bare check: a bare check at a projected coordinate refuses, because the projection rewrites `plan_tree.json`, `plan_tree.sha256` and `producer_contract.json` through a different serializer, and treating those receipts by bare check would have failed the pre-arm gate for the entire `_v4` family. THE HARD PART took two rounds: admitting a flagless generator on an AST NAME SCAN (absence of the identifier `preserve_current_frozen_bytes`) proves nothing, because an echo can be written under any other name — the first delta re-audit executed exactly that attack and watched the classifier label a tamper `regenerated`. Fix round 2 made flagless generators DEFAULT-DENIED, admitted only by exact SHA-256 membership in a closed, minimal allowlist of reviewed historical generators whose digests are derived from local Git at the coordinates the ordinal-1 sources name; the name scan may now only REFUSE, never admit. Regression-pinned at both boundaries: the foreign-identifier echo attack is refused, an allowlisted historical generator still authenticates. Acceptance evidence (a) is `what-check-proves.md`; (b) is the non-tautological derivation plus its regressions, verdict A94 MET by the second delta re-audit (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/delta2/report.md`, no blocker findings). `_v4` re-verified from post-cure code — default-deny is exactly the shape that could have broken it: all three emitting `_v3` generators classify explicit-flag, projected authoring and anchor+replay pass, custody scripts unchanged, 99/99 committed receipts still validate, +2.310 s median per pack. NOT done here, recorded for the magistrate as follow-ups from the second delta re-audit: D2 (the contract narrates echo-vs-regeneration but shows no literal before/after bytes, and `PACK_DIGEST_DOMAIN` and the pre-authoring invariant are used as criteria before they are taught), D3 (a cleanup error raised BEFORE removal leaves the temporary checkout on disk; both boundaries still govern-refuse, and the committed regression cleans up before raising so it cannot see the leak), D4 (a blobless partial/promisor clone lazy-fetched four missing blobs and returned PASS instead of failing closed — a PRE-EXISTING property of `_historical_pack_tree`, newly discovered rather than newly introduced, and the most consequential of the four), and D6 (the reviewed S-1 manifest pins builder digest `29335e6f…` while the current builder and its sidecar agree on `d72c1560…` — the r4 runsheet generates a current BASE manifest so operation is unaffected, but the cited review record is false, which matters for the imminent mint). Custody: `docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/`. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:107:| SUPERSESSION-DUP-REFUSAL-01 | P1 Phase Gate | 2026-08-27 | Rule on and then implement write-time refusal in the supersession recorder, which appended silent duplicate records when run more than once for a member and voided campaign membership downstream | Landed as PR #206 (`36dcdd76`). Ruling-first, as the row required. **D-156** was authored and landed by the magistrate BEFORE any implementation, on a ruling packet (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/supersession-dup-ruling-packet.md`) built from a Sol xhigh read-only design seat plus lieutenant re-verification of every file:line; a blind Fable refuter then returned SOUND on both lenses over D-156's five premises (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/supersession-dup-refuter-fable.md`). Ruled semantics, implemented verbatim: any *recognizable* row (exact `record_type` OR exact `schema_version`) already carrying this `bundle_id` in the **target log** refuses, keyed on `bundle_id` within one log, checked inside the held `campaign.lock` BEFORE the candidate row is constructed and before quarantine bytes are read — and **presence, not validity, occupies the slot**: a recognizable-but-invalid row refuses just as hard, because an invalid competing disposition must never license a second one. Refusal surface follows the `LaunchLineageError` precedent: `SupersessionRecorderError(ValueError)` carrying `.reason_code`, validated against a **sibling** registry `SUPERSESSION_RECORDER_REASON_CODES` (deliberately NOT a widening of `LAUNCH_LINEAGE_REASON_CODES`, so the paper's disjoint-vocabulary claim at `docs/paper/draft-v1.md:742` stays true), wire values `campaign_occurrence_supersession_already_recorded` and `campaign_occurrence_supersession_log_unreadable`, printed through the one existing `error: {reason_code}: {msg}` path at exit 2. The refuter's R-1 residual was real and material: the guard's first draft read `load_campaign_log_rows`, which *tolerates one recognized final tear*, while the consumers read through `supersession_entry_validation_results`, which fails closed to `None` — so a **torn final line that is a partial supersession row** would have been invisible to the guard and fatal to the consumer; FIX-1 drives the refusal from both readers. A later magistrate amendment gave that branch its own truthful sibling code `campaign_occurrence_supersession_log_unreadable`, because refusing as "already recorded" when nothing was recorded misreports the condition and `docs/paper/draft-v1.md:742` stakes a published claim on refusal names being the thing that is true. The fresh read-only delta re-audit (ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES, no blockers) then caught the amendment's own rationale being false in the same way: the message and runbook claimed appending would produce an unusable log, but `append_log` quarantines a recognized torn tail, truncates, and appends (`scripts/run_campaign.py:1405-1416`), so the append would in fact succeed. The truthful objection replaced it — quarantining an operator's torn evidence is a custody decision that must be deliberate and recorded, not a side effect of a supersession write. Six regressions, none redundant: identical-args rerun (API + CLI surface, byte-identical log); **third-occurrence rerun with a different `selected_occurrence`** (the divergence-creating write — whole-window membership would otherwise ACCEPT it while the cooldown join refuses); invalid-existing-row; different-`bundle_id` still allowed (scope boundary); unidentifiable-`bundle_id` log blocked globally (3 subtests); torn recognizable final row. **Defect-shaped proof executed**: guard neutralized → 7 failures across 5 of the 6 methods, only the scope-boundary test passing as designed; guard restored → 6 OK. Suites: `tests.test_run_campaign` Ran 263 OK; `tests.test_analysis_integration` Ran 102 OK (preservation — D-156 ruled NO consumer change and the consumer regressions prove none happened). Also landed: the runbook §11 refusal-table row, the once-per-log rule, the ruled escape hatch (Q1 = A: fresh runs root or non-claim disposition; same-root chained recovery unsupported), and the **mandatory** per-`bundle_id` detection scan — mandatory because the existing D-093 audit compares TOTALS (`raw_count == validated_count`) and therefore reports two *valid* same-bundle rows as clean, blind to this exact defect. NOT done here, deliberately: no consumer change, no historical byte repair (Q2 = A: preserve and refuse), and the two residual rows are DRAFTS only in `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/supersession-queued-rows-draft.md` — `SUPERSESSION-CHAINED-RECOVERY-01` (Q1-B) and `SUPERSESSION-CROSS-CONSUMER-DIVERGENCE-01` (Q4-B) — awaiting magistrate registration, not registered by this PR. |
TASK_QUEUE.md:108:| FROZEN-RECEIPT-CONSTANT-STALE-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Stop successor-family PACK_AUTHENTICATION from resting on `CURRENT_FROZEN_RECEIPT_SHA256`, the generator constant that names the PREDECESSOR's freeze receipt | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Landed on PR #214 (branch `fix/packauth-soundness-rows`; gauntlet: design consult → implementation → independent audit → fix round → delta re-audit). The staleness is structural, not an accident: `embedded_generator_bytes()` emits a successor generator by substituting only `CURRENT_FAMILY_SUFFIX`, so every successor family is born one generation behind and `_v4` — emitted from the `_v3` generators — will name the `_v2` freeze-0002 digest too. Executed across all nine packs (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-26-t26-s3/characterization.md`, replayable via `replay-characterization.sh`): the three ordinal-1 packs match their own receipt and pass a bare `--check`; all six successors exit 1 with `generation failed: the current frozen identity requires preserve mode`. ADOPTED RULING: the constant is NOT refreshed per generation and the authentication path stops depending on it. Refreshing is impossible rather than merely undesirable — a successor generator is emitted before its own freeze receipt exists, so the digest it would need does not yet exist, and editing the generator after the mint would change already-frozen pack bytes (D-153 would then force a new family generation). The ruling is recorded normatively in `docs/contracts/receipt_histsem_verifier.md` §'Adopted A93 ruling' (dated 2026-08-26) and pinned by `test_frozen_receipt_constant_variants_do_not_change_the_authentication_verdict`, which holds one derivation fixed, varies the constant through absent / matches-current / names-predecessor / unrelated / computed / duplicated / malformed forms and requires an IDENTICAL authentication verdict with only diagnostic differences. The constant is now read by a TOTAL `ast.parse`/`ast.literal_eval` extractor that never raises and never reaches the verdict; its relation is recorded with `authentication_dependency: false`. An earlier shape that refused a flagless generator merely because the constant existed was caught by the independent audit (F1, blocker) and removed — preserve CAPABILITY, not the constant, now selects the invocation. NOT done here: PACKAUTH-PRESERVE-TAUTOLOGY-01, which shares the branch and stays open on the delta re-audit's D1 blocker. A binding `docs/decision_log.md` entry for this ruling is OWED at the merge gate (magistrate's act). |
TASK_QUEUE.md:109:| MINT-CHECKOUT-DECLARATION-01 | P2 Next Slice | 2026-08-27 | Build the mint-time measurement-checkout declaration check that D-154 R-3 re-sites the locality lens onto, so the one real event the absolute pack_root comparison ever caught is caught once, at mint, against a declared checkout | No phase exit-checklist matrix row exists. Merged via #208 (squash SHA to be recorded at merge): `generate_freeze_receipt` takes a REQUIRED keyword-only `measurement_checkout`, and both production CLIs (`scripts/generate_arm_readiness.py freeze`, `scripts/author_arm_readiness_evidence.py`) take a required `--measurement-checkout`; the gate compares the resolved repository owning the pack against the strictly-resolved declaration, fires on the CREATE path only (after idempotent replay returns, so R-3's "once, AT MINT" holds) and before any byte is written (so a refusal spends no freeze ordinal). New reason code `readiness_r1_measurement_checkout` (role `MEASUREMENT_CHECKOUT`, type `CUSTODY`) with its ninth ruled-registry `refusal_vocabulary` entry; load-closure pinned in BOTH directions and the `READINESS_REASON_CODES` census moved 55 → 56 deliberately. All four acceptance items VERIFIED by an independent read-only audit: refuse-outside/mint-inside, two-directional registry closure, a T10 `wtTXN`-class regression across two real git repositories through the real CLI by subprocess (exact reason code, and proof no receipt namespace was created), and supplied-never-inferred (no env var, `window.env`, cwd, `REPO_ROOT`, or pack-derived fallback exists on the declared side). Mutation kills recorded for the gate, both closure directions, and the gate PLACEMENT (moving it above the replay branch goes red). The live `docs/phase_2/window_runbook.md` freeze command was repaired in the same PR; ten dated historical command records were deliberately left unchanged. NOT done here, on the record: the transaction runbook's PROMPT 4–6 text (`docs/process_traces/2026-08-22-t20/rea