docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:1:# Research-question coverage against the frozen `_v5` campaign, the transfer fiducial (known-gap diagnostic), and the three-model ladder
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:5:This is the coverage map Ed requested and decision D-163 (the ruling on what follows `_v5`: the inserted-gap fiducial and the three-model decode ladder) ordered (`docs/decision_log.md:10336-10348`). It puts every live row in `docs/research_question_registry.md` beside the additional identifiers retained only in `docs/research_question_bank.md`, then asks what the frozen `_v5` campaign on `mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` and `mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit`, the first post-campaign transfer-fiducial diagnostic, the three-model ladder whose D-163 model set is unresolved under `_v5`, or evidence already retained at the desk can honestly answer. The live registry supplies current type, status, and claim ceiling; the bank supplies the historical question wording, rejected upgrades, and the ten identifiers that were folded into live rows rather than given their own registry rows.
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:9:A **bundle** is the per-run evidence folder—power trace, events, outputs, and metadata—that the reducer, the analysis program, consumes. A **holdout** or **held-out request** is deliberately excluded from fitting and used only to test prediction. A **smoke run** is a small feasibility test, and a **shim** is a small adapter between the external runner and JouleWise. Greedy, sampled, and beam decoding are output-selection strategies: greedy always chooses the most probable next token, sampling draws randomly, and beam decoding keeps several candidate continuations. HumanEval is a public code-generation benchmark of programming problems; FLORES is a public multilingual translation benchmark that presents the same sentences in many languages; and **tokenizer fertility** means the number of tokens produced per word or character for a language. AXI names the project’s architecture-extension stream. A state-space/attention hybrid combines recurrent state updates with attention layers, rather than using attention alone.
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:13:The registry/bank status is copied, not reconsidered: **promoted** means the question owns a named project slot; **banked** means viable but not promoted; **candidate** means proposed and bounded; **killed** means deliberately rejected; **answered-L1** means answered only at the registry’s limited descriptive claim level; and **candidate (C-023)** is the whole-project review’s candidate class.
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:15:Every coverage cell uses exactly one of these labels. The letter is only a reading aid; the words are controlling.
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:17:- **A. `answered by _v5`** — the frozen three-pack design on `mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` and `mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit` will answer the row if collection and governed close-out succeed.
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:19:- **C. `answerable by ladder`** — the D-163 decode-only 0.5B/1.5B/7B ladder as ruled predates D-164, and its model set is unresolved under `_v5` (`docs/decision_log.md:191`).
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:23:- **G. `answerable with this instrument, no route scheduled`** — this Mac, sampler, bundle format, and floor machinery could answer the row, but `_v5`, the fiducial, the ladder, and retained desk evidence do not. The short reason states the additional cells and measurement night or nights required.
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:24:- **H. `answerable by the _v6 scored leg`** — Ed’s scored benchmark leg uses GSM8K, eight items per member, and a pinned checker; accuracy is a set property under the AP-5 / C5-1.9 quarantine because training-data contamination cannot be ruled out. It is built at the desk during `_v5` and run post-campaign after the fiducial night (`docs/decision_log.md:193`).
docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:26:The `_v5` rows below cite the checked-in `*_v3` predecessor pack shapes. The contrast pack has a checked-in **analysis manifest**—the predeclared instructions for reducing and testing its data—at `configs/campaigns/d117_contrast_qwen25_1p5b_vs_7b_v3/analysis_manifest_v3.json`; the two floor directories have plan trees but no `analysis_manifest_v3.json`. No separately named `_v5` pack configuration or fifth-generation freeze record was found in this worktree. The predecessor `_v4` project task record and final ruling say that the real transaction would have created freeze records from these three predecessor campaign families (`docs/process/state_kernel.json:4500-4548`; `docs/process_traces/2026-08-20-go-session/rulings-r5-consolidation.md:72-104`), but D-164 says `_v4` is never collected. The `_v5` pack re-pins the models to `mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` and `mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit` per D-164 and is not yet in this tree (`docs/decision_log.md:191`). The checked-in program that validates manifest generation is `joulewise/analysis_manifest_v3.py`.
