docs/research_question_coverage-2026-08-28.md:61:| RQ-ATTRIBUTION-DOMINANCE | Does phase-boundary uncertainty contribute more than repeat-to-repeat scatter to each phase-cell resolution bound? | research question | candidate | A. `answered by _v5` — if collected, each prefill and decode floor cell independently compares its repeatability term after the small-sample safety multiplier with the exact maximum false effect over the allowed phase-boundary positions. The falsifier is now the pre-registered dominance ratio R—the corner-widened unguarded bound (“corner-widened” means using the worst allowed combination of boundary shifts) divided by the point unguarded bound (“point” means using the nominal fitted boundaries)—with R ≥ 2 required per component per cell and all required to pass; the common-mode ratio is disclosed, and R_cm < 2 withdraws the dominance sentence. | Live row: `docs/research_question_registry.md:82`; question and superseded item-34 falsifier: `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/paper-goal-consult/03-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md:65-78`; controlling per-component predicate and reported quantities: `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/paper-goal-consult/03-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md:265-274`; item 34 superseded by the controlling ratio ruling: `docs/decision_log.md:192`; implementation: `joulewise/detection_floor.py:689-718`; `joulewise/detection_floor.py:735-841`; `joulewise/floor_extraction.py:2290-2300`; `joulewise/floor_extraction.py:2749-2759`; fixed pack identities: `configs/campaigns/d117_floor_qwen25_1p5b_v3/plan_tree.json:266-286`; `configs/campaigns/d117_floor_qwen25_7b_v3/plan_tree.json:267-287`; partial: transfer from calibration pulses to real inference remains an assumption, tested only by the later diagnostic fiducial: `docs/process/state_kernel.json:4354-4367`; historical paper framing only: `docs/paper/draft-v1.md:19-21`. | §1: “does phase-boundary attribution rather than run-to-run scatter dominate the resolution bound” |
