docs/decision_log.md:181:| D-154 | `pack_root` LOCALITY RULING (magistrate synthesis 2026-08-25 over two cross-model seats, Opus contract lens + gpt-5.6-sol xhigh; trace `docs/process_traces/2026-08-25-packroot-consult/03-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md` + both seats): R-1 successor-scoped repo-relative structural pack identity at generations ≥ `family_publication_first_generation` (`_v3` and earlier keep absolute semantics, so the 2026-08-20 location ruling is not silently superseded); R-2 each refusal detail true per branch, no new reason codes; R-3 the locality lens re-sited to MINT time (not retired); R-4 estate 7 STRUCK as instrument failure, its positives retained as executability evidence only; R-5 the implementation gauntlet. Landed as PR #192 after a fresh cross-model refuter. BACKFILLED 2026-08-27 (T26): the ruling was custodied and cited as D-154 from 2026-08-25 but never indexed here — a consistency-sweep miss, not a new decision. | adopted (magistrate synthesis over two seats; backfilled index) |
docs/decision_log.md:182:| D-155 | NR ADJUDICATION PACKAGE — the thirteen pre-window rulings for the real `_v4` transaction (magistrate synthesis 2026-08-26 over a mechanically-assembled packet and TWO independent adjudication seats, Opus and gpt-5.6-sol xhigh, both recorded verbatim beside it; trace `docs/process_traces/2026-08-22-t20/nr-synthesis-ruling.md` + `nr-seat-opus.md` + `nr-seat-sol.md`). Convergence was near-total, and both seats independently found two facts the packet missed: a TWIN terminal-review trailer parser at `scripts/capture_t0_step.py:288-316` (a cure at the evidence collector alone would still have refused at the first T-0 capture step — the 'another missed call site' signature, caught at the desk instead of mid-transaction), and `.claude/settings.local.json` allow-rules that could suppress or bypass the D-150(1) live prompts. ELEVEN OF THIRTEEN RULED, ten of them zero-code. (NR-11) branch D at BOTH parsers: `PASS`/`Tree-Oid` stay exactly-once, `Pack-Sha256` becomes non-empty, duplicate-free, membership of the arming pack's digest; zero refusal-registry cost; five-case regressions at each site; three-trailer producer in `window_runbook.md` §5C; no zero-code path exists (branch E verified mechanically empty three times). (NR-12) branch B: ONE magistrate-executed (D-150b), tree-preserving attestation commit AFTER the mint; `ATTESTATION_HEAD` = published head, `PINSET_MINT_HEAD` = allowlist-closure/`hS` head; every step naming 'the head' says which. (NR-3) branch A, push-then-build, with Phase E reordered E1 build -> E3 render -> E4 delegated confirmation/`hC` -> E2 verify -> E5 promote (a publication-phase verify REQUIRES the confirmation pair); r4-3 amended with a dated marker, never silently. (NR-2) branch A: pull-into-dev -> push origin -> fetch-back, four-way equality asserted by RUNNING `reviewed_main`, never by eye; a fetch is licensed inside the freeze span, a commit/push/branch-move is not; the invented `file://` form dropped. (NR-1) branch A: `/Users/edr/JouleWise-measurement-20260813` fast-forwarded (ancestry verified); `-20260818` rejected on three grounds including its blanket allow rule; a fresh checkout is the NAMED FALLBACK if the venv relock cannot reach the lock. (NR-4) branch A: marker build AND verify `--phase publication`; the §1.3 candidate manifest is STILL PRODUCED because C9 consumes it for custody-tool digests. (NR-13) code guard landing BEFORE Phase C1 — the binding gate is the changed-set window, not the freeze span: custody-external sentinel, refuse-before-write, byte-identical out-of-span behaviour, two-branch regression; D-150a visibility unaffected (the channel is the push notification, not the git push). (NR-6) branch B: dry-run ceremony x3, NO real arm; `file-09-probe P1/P2/P3` STRUCK AS SPECIFIED (P3 requires the arm B-4 forbids) and replaced by named assertions over the dry-run receipts, with P3 discharged at the shakedown GO receipt and arm-side U11 at the shakedown arm; the Sol seat's read-only reformulation of P3 recorded as DISSENT and declined — renaming an unsatisfiable ruled property to a satisfiable weaker one is the quiet-weakening shape this process refuses. (NR-7) D-153 A4 governs; condition 5 RE-SCOPED, not struck, into two sub-intervals (mint -> first consuming arm: no arms; first consuming arm -> fixation: the campaign's claim-bearing arms under marker + table); ONE home `MAGISTRATE-RULING-O1.md` condition 5, with the D-151 index row clarified as a pointer. (NR-8) mechanical campaign-close declaration by the magistrate with an ED ESCAPE for early termination/waivers/abandonment; canonical `campaign-close.json` in transaction custody; STRICT record order — declaration -> freeze-off -> notification -> THE FIXATION COMMIT FIRST -> only then any bookkeeping. (NR-10) six ruled prompts stand PLUS a mandatory pre-window prompt inventory (ALLOW/ASK/DENY table with exact strings, cwd and the `python3` vs `python` spelling trap); if the broad allows would swallow a licensed command, ED narrows them — no agent self-modification of settings. OPERATOR FIXES: fresh-venv relock (preserve `.venv` as `.venv.pre-v4`, rebuild from the lock's canonical constraints form) accepted on an EMPTY 37-line diff, not a version print, with wheel-unavailability falling back to the fresh checkout; and the step-6 contract prose amended to record the D-150b standing delegation with independent recomputation of `hM`/`hS` (`authority: ED` / `decision: YES` unchanged). STILL OPEN: NR-5 (does the real lane re-run the §4 probe battery) and NR-9's notification cadence, which is Ed's one-word question (recommendation: immediate). PRE-WINDOW WORKLIST W-0..W-9 in the synthesis; earliest credible transaction night 2026-08-28, gated on W-2 clearing its gauntlet first-pass. | adopted (magistrate synthesis over two independent seats) |
docs/decision_log.md:183:| D-156 | SUPERSESSION WRITE-TIME REFUSAL (SUPERSESSION-DUP-REFUSAL-01 ruling, magistrate 2026-08-27 over a Sol xhigh read-only seat + Opus lieutenant packet, both agreeing on every axis; packet `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/supersession-dup-ruling-packet.md`): the supersession recorder REFUSES, before row construction, any write whose `bundle_id` already has a recognizable row in the target campaign log — unconditionally, keyed on `bundle_id` within one log, with NO requirement that the existing row validate (an invalid competing disposition never licenses a second write); registered reason code `campaign_occurrence_supersession_already_recorded` on the existing `LaunchLineageError` pattern; no consumer change; no byte repair owed. Facts the ruling rests on: same-bytes idempotency is not an available option (`utc_timestamp()` is inside `entry_sha256`); the immediate double-run is already fail-closed in both consumers (cooldown join and whole-window membership each demand exactly one row); a later THIRD occurrence produces a cross-consumer divergence (membership selects, cooldown refuses, identical bytes); D-093's supersession audit is blind to it (compares totals only); zero supersession rows exist in any reachable campaign log. Residuals: Q1 later failure of an already-selected occurrence → A (fresh root / non-claim disposition) now, chained-supersession schema minted as a QUEUED row (latest-wins rejected on ruled grounds — `whole_window_verdict_conflict`); Q2 historical duplicates → A (preserve and refuse; retraction design separately; rewrite rejected); Q3 off-machine Window B/C per-`bundle_id` scan → A MANDATORY before any consumption of those corpora, documented in runbook §11; Q4 the cross-consumer divergence → B its own queued row (a fail-closed consumer change does not ride a write-time-guard PR); Q5 this entry is the ruling the row's acceptance requires. | adopted (magistrate; seat + lieutenant unanimous) |
docs/decision_log.md:187:| D-160 | THE SMOKE CORPUS (magistrate 2026-08-27 over THREE blind seats after the standing escalation trigger fired on three consecutive falsified evidence-path premises; trace `docs/process_traces/2026-08-27-t26/smoke-corpus-consult/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md` + seats): no path yields a claim-consumable synthetic bundle without new production seams (fake-collector seam is a scissor: mock ⇒ `mock_telemetry_claim_ineligible` at inputs.py:2753 and `capture_pipeline_absent`; powermetrics ⇒ `bundle_strict_invalid`); the tier-2 replay seam is not CLI-reachable and costs two custody surfaces; the floor path is CLOSED BY CONSTRUCTION (`inputs.py:3931` refuses `calibration_scope == "smoke"` as `cell_not_claim_ready`); and NO PRODUCER EXISTS for the finalizer's `--bracket-binding` file. RULINGS: R-1 no synthetic clean leg before the night and no floor-rule relaxation — the desk smoke is W-11 (#211) + Unit B, proving contract defects fail loudly, not a clean pass; R-2 the clean end-to-end proof is the LIVE ~20-minute run on a real tiny quarantined generation (Ed's machine, evening before; zero seams); R-3 BRACKET-BINDING-CLI-01 upgraded to a pre-CLOSE blocker (no producer at all), assigned to S10 now; R-4 PIPELINE-SMOKE-TIER2-01 registered post-`_v4` with constraints; R-5 evidence-path rulings are made only after a seat has executed the path or proven it cannot. | adopted (magistrate over three blind seats) |
docs/decision_log.md:188:| D-161 | THREAT-MODEL PRUNE (Ed, 2026-08-27, in-session, ratifying the magistrate's three-point proposal: "yes to all 3. right instincts"): the in-process adversary is already OUT of the threat model (D-139 A1; D-148 (6)) and the paper's §7 states a single trusted operator, so custody mechanisms whose ONLY defended-against actor is the trusted operator touching a file are over-engineering; this week they cost the operator three hand edits and blocked the mint twice. RULINGS: (1) the reviewed pinset gets a REVIEWED REFRESH LANE (`--refresh-row`, re-derives a row from the committed tree by the verifier's own code path, prints the diff, lands as an ordinary PR); the "no update lane" test becomes "no UNREVIEWED update" — stream S14; (2) THREAT-MODEL-PRUNE-01: enumerate from code (three-seat consult) every refusal whose only actor is the trusted operator and downgrade it to WARN-AND-RECORD or retire it; fail-closed STAYS where the failure is PHYSICS/EVIDENCE or PRE-REGISTRATION (missing calibration, unresolved anchor, absent floor, stale drift evidence, unfrozen plan, post-hoc analysis choice); prunes that the frozen `_v4` runbook or estate 11 depend on wait until after the transaction; (3) the paper's §7 says the repository is tamper-EVIDENT for the operator's own benefit, not tamper-PROOF against anyone (lands with the `_v4` fills). Ed's hands are no longer required for the W-10 pin. | adopted (Ed) |
docs/decision_log.md:192:| D-165 | THE FALSIFIER (magistrate 2026-08-28 over three blind seats; cold gate `docs/process_traces/2026-08-28-falsifier-consult/06-COLD-GATE-RULING.md`; reverses paper-goal item 34, amends item 28): the registered dominance predicate (`detection_floor.py:806-843`) is near-vacuous — true for any positive width once max|r| ≥ 2.372·s_r — and survives only as the cell label. A dominance RATIO R = corner-widened unguarded bound / point unguarded bound is pre-registered into the `_v5` pack as a `dominance_criterion` sub-object in each contrast's `floor_estimator_registration` (hashed into `frozen_semantics_sha256`; injected in the generator's contrast dict, never the common-mode registration), gate **R ≥ 2** per component per cell, all must pass, comparative kind. Common-mode R_cm is mandatory disclosure; **R_cm < 2** withdraws the dominance sentence; S15 chooses pre-mint how R_cm is derived (widths are composed and destroyed at `floor_extraction.py:481-489`). ONE protocol-first title fixed before collection, "attribution-limited" a gate-contingent subtitle, branch rule disclosed in one methods sentence. Opus finding (absolute component may charge a common shift that cancels) → Sol xhigh bench check before the `_v5` freeze. "Minted" is evidenced only by the clone-proof artifact. | adopted (magistrate + cold gate) |
docs/decision_log.md:193:| D-166 | THE WORKLOAD (magistrate 2026-08-28 over three blind seats, Ed-prompted; trace `docs/process_traces/2026-08-28-workload-consult/04-MAGISTRATE-RULING.md`): the synthetic prompt is replaced, the fixed-shape per-cell-floor machinery kept. `_v5` decode arm = real pinned prompts rendered through the Qwen3 chat template with thinking OFF (token IDs pinned), greedy, forced 512 — no harness change; `_v5` prefill length fixed from the G2 shakedown record: the shortest of 512/1024/2048/4096 prompt tokens at which every one of ≥5 small-model G2-a probe members shows a prefill overlapping-power-record count ≥ 5 (equivalently `sample_count_margin` ≥ 2 over the reducer floor `MIN_PHASE_SAMPLES` = 3; the floor is the physical rule, the +2 a declared pre-registration safety factor; a rung with no small-model members is unevaluable and cannot be selected; large-model probes recorded, non-gating). If no rung clears, the prefill arm is still collected at 4096 and the printed result distinguishes refusals honestly: a reducer refusal (`not_resolvable_sample_count`, count < 3) prints as itself; a resolvable count of 3–4 prints as the PRE-REGISTRATION refusal ("below the pre-registered count floor of 5") with the reducer's resolvable result disclosed alongside; Holm family stays m = 2. Pre-registered before the mint; the pre-registration object pins the ladder, the count floor, the `MIN_PHASE_SAMPLES` consistency check, the selection expression, and the G2-a record hash it selected from. [AMENDED by cold gate + refuter + ratification 2026-08-30, `docs/process_traces/2026-08-30-prefill-margin-coldgate/` 01–03: "margin ≥5" disambiguated to count ≥ 5; ladder extended to 4096; refusal branch split; G2-a sweep (≥5 members/rung) made the selection's precondition.] Ed's scored benchmark leg (GSM8K k=8 same items per member, cap 384, pinned checker, 4-way outcome table, accuracy a set property under AP-5/C5-1.9 quarantine — contamination unmitigable) is `_v6`: built at the desk DURING the `_v5` campaign (5–8 Sol-days, stream WORKLOAD-SCORED-01), run post-campaign after the fiducial night, with `affine_mod_ladder_v1` as the contamination-free control leg. Calendar unchanged: transaction ≈ 09-01/02. | adopted (magistrate) |
